Toho Co., Ltd.
TMS Entertainment Ltd.

00:00:18.540 --> 00:00:22.580
Original Work
Aoyama Gosho
Serialized in Shogakukan's "Weekly Shonen Sunday"

00:00:30.380 --> 00:00:32.720
Marina Bay Sands

00:00:31.210 --> 00:00:32.050
Hey, gal.

00:00:57.470 --> 00:00:59.280
Did I make you wait?

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:01.910
This is a strange place to meet.

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:04.120
Can we talk in Japanese...

00:01:04.120 --> 00:01:05.670
So that people around us won't listen?

00:01:07.250 --> 00:01:10.340
Sherilyn Tan (40)
Attorney-at-Law

00:01:07.350 --> 00:01:10.650
You can't do that weird behavior of yours if you're attracting attention, right?

00:01:10.650 --> 00:01:12.440
That's an awfully terrible way of putting it.

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:14.010
Leon Lowe (43)
Business Consultant

00:01:12.440 --> 00:01:15.240
You're practically making it sound
as if I have my eyes set on you.

00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:16.180
Am I wrong?

00:01:16.180 --> 00:01:20.010
I feel that I've built up a
good relationship with you as a friend...

00:01:20.010 --> 00:01:22.620
Cut the unnecessary chitchat.

00:01:22.620 --> 00:01:25.770
Just give me your answer
about my proposition.

00:01:25.770 --> 00:01:28.710
Yes or no?

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:35.170
Before I answer that...

00:01:35.170 --> 00:01:38.390
Allow me to guess
what you just ordered.

00:01:38.390 --> 00:01:39.740
Iced tea.

00:01:39.740 --> 00:01:42.350
No, that's not it.
Champagne...?

00:01:42.350 --> 00:01:45.430
No, wine.
Not red, but white.

00:01:45.430 --> 00:01:46.910
A well-chilled Meursault.

00:01:46.910 --> 00:01:48.690
Here is your Meursault.

00:01:49.310 --> 00:01:52.400
H-How did you know?

00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:54.760
I read your mind.

00:01:54.760 --> 00:01:55.340
Um, excuse me...

00:01:55.340 --> 00:01:56.510
I don't need it!

00:01:59.510 --> 00:02:00.550
Ah, wait a second.

00:02:01.990 --> 00:02:03.060
What do you want?!

00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:04.970
My answer is no.

00:02:15.190 --> 00:02:16.320
Thanks for the help.

00:02:30.880 --> 00:02:32.130
First floor.

00:02:53.020 --> 00:02:54.520
Hey, are you okay...?

00:03:12.630 --> 00:03:13.460
W-What?!

00:03:21.430 --> 00:03:22.800
Please be calm!

00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:24.300
Follow our instructions...

00:03:30.180 --> 00:03:31.100
Hey, wait!

00:03:31.890 --> 00:03:32.940
What are you doing?

00:03:33.940 --> 00:03:35.820
Preserving the scene of the crime.

00:03:35.820 --> 00:03:36.690
Otherwise...

00:03:36.690 --> 00:03:39.490
This will be trampled over, right?

00:03:54.290 --> 00:03:55.210
Sir.

00:03:55.460 --> 00:03:57.090
The one I called?

00:03:57.090 --> 00:03:58.380
He's already inside.

00:03:58.630 --> 00:03:59.460
Thanks.

00:04:01.470 --> 00:04:03.340
Sorry to make you wait, Rishi!

00:04:03.510 --> 00:04:05.010
Inspector Aidan!

00:04:05.180 --> 00:04:06.970
Thank you for calling me.

00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:10.310
The incident happened
at the shopping mall ahead.

00:04:08.970 --> 00:04:12.020
Mark Aidan (38)
Assistant Inspector of the
Singapore Police Force

00:04:10.640 --> 00:04:13.270
This case could be a little tricky.

00:04:14.810 --> 00:04:18.230
That Leon Lowe first discovered the body.

00:04:18.610 --> 00:04:18.980
Oh...

00:04:18.980 --> 00:04:19.980
Mr. Lowe!

00:04:20.990 --> 00:04:23.820
You were his favorite student, right?

00:04:23.820 --> 00:04:26.820
Could you ask him not to interfere too much?

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:28.830
I can't ask him that.

00:04:28.830 --> 00:04:30.290
I'll go say hello!

00:04:31.450 --> 00:04:32.620
Mr. Lowe!

00:04:32.790 --> 00:04:35.290
Rishi! It has been a while.

00:04:35.290 --> 00:04:36.040
Yes!

00:04:38.990 --> 00:04:40.680
Let's speak in Japanese.

00:04:40.680 --> 00:04:41.550
Sure.

00:04:41.550 --> 00:04:45.720
I hear you're working
as a private reserve officer now?

00:04:45.720 --> 00:04:47.070
You've sure
moved up in the world.

00:04:46.140 --> 00:04:49.140
Rishi Ramanathan (29)
Reserve Officer

00:04:47.070 --> 00:04:51.240
As my instructor, you pounded
criminal behavior psychology into my head...

00:04:51.240 --> 00:04:52.810
So this is all thanks
to you, Leon-sensei.

00:04:52.810 --> 00:04:55.040
Please stop referring
to me as your instructor.

00:04:55.040 --> 00:04:56.900
I'm just a civilian now.

00:04:56.900 --> 00:04:57.860
At any rate...

00:04:57.860 --> 00:05:00.820
I never would have thought
the killer had planted bombs.

00:05:00.820 --> 00:05:02.340
And the car that was bombed...

00:05:02.340 --> 00:05:05.130
Belonged to the victim,
Sherilyn Tan-san.

00:05:05.130 --> 00:05:07.870
She was an excellent
defense attorney, after all...

00:05:07.870 --> 00:05:09.870
So I'm sure there were those
who held a grudge against her.

00:05:09.870 --> 00:05:11.740
She could have also been
associating with someone dangerous...

00:05:11.740 --> 00:05:13.370
Is the inspector there?!

00:05:14.210 --> 00:05:16.250
Excuse me! Make way!

00:05:16.670 --> 00:05:17.710
What's going on?

00:05:17.710 --> 00:05:19.840
There's something on the elevator wall.

00:05:20.630 --> 00:05:21.210
What?!

00:05:21.960 --> 00:05:23.260
What is this?

00:05:31.280 --> 00:05:32.520
Wha...?!

00:05:56.600 --> 00:05:57.830
Absolutely not.

00:05:58.900 --> 00:06:00.840
Please, can't you
just do this for me?!

00:06:00.840 --> 00:06:02.660
No means no.

00:06:02.660 --> 00:06:03.150
I'm begging you!

00:06:03.150 --> 00:06:04.760
What's going on, you two?

00:06:04.760 --> 00:06:08.780
He says he wants to use that one medicine
to go back to his original form again.

00:06:08.780 --> 00:06:12.620
He <i>just</i> went through a terrible
experience during his school trip, too...

00:06:12.620 --> 00:06:15.450
Even then, I managed to make it
through what happened one way or another.

00:06:15.450 --> 00:06:17.850
So I'll be fine!
Please give me the medicine!

00:06:17.850 --> 00:06:20.020
Absolutely not!

00:06:20.880 --> 00:06:22.520
And just where
does he plan on going?

00:06:22.520 --> 00:06:24.050
Singapore.

00:06:24.050 --> 00:06:25.530
It's because of this, Professor!

00:06:25.530 --> 00:06:27.970
That one guy's going to
be in this championship!

00:06:27.970 --> 00:06:29.200
The one with
no losses in 400 matches!

00:06:29.720 --> 00:06:31.050
Oh!

00:06:31.050 --> 00:06:32.950
You mean Kyogoku Makoto-kun?

00:06:32.950 --> 00:06:36.220
So Sonoko suggested
going to see that match.

00:06:36.220 --> 00:06:40.750
And I was invited to go along
with old man Kogoro and Ran...

00:06:40.750 --> 00:06:42.960
But I can't leave
the country looking like this.

00:06:42.960 --> 00:06:44.090
That's right...

00:06:44.090 --> 00:06:46.460
Because your passport is for Shinichi.

00:06:46.460 --> 00:06:48.650
So please, Haibara!

00:06:48.650 --> 00:06:49.760
Give. It. Up.

00:06:49.760 --> 00:06:51.020
Oh, come on...

00:06:51.020 --> 00:06:53.580
It might be best
to just give up this time...

00:06:53.580 --> 00:06:56.750
Aw...
I really wanted to go.

00:06:56.930 --> 00:06:58.960
Don't be so disappointed!

00:06:58.960 --> 00:07:01.670
Alright, here's my first shot
at cheering you up!

00:07:01.670 --> 00:07:03.380
What...?
You're doing this <i>already</i>?!

00:07:03.380 --> 00:07:06.670
Tada!
Here comes the quiz!

00:07:06.670 --> 00:07:10.950
What is the single,
most popular event in Singapore?

00:07:10.950 --> 00:07:12.950
1.
Singing the
National Anthem

00:07:10.950 --> 00:07:12.950
1. Singing the national anthem.

00:07:12.950 --> 00:07:13.030
2.
Celebrating the
Lunar New Year

00:07:12.950 --> 00:07:15.560
2. Celebrating the Lunar New Year.

00:07:15.560 --> 00:07:17.930
3. Flying the national flag.

00:07:15.660 --> 00:07:15.910
3.
Flying the
National Flag

00:07:17.930 --> 00:07:20.500
4. The fireworks display at Marina Bay.

00:07:18.040 --> 00:07:18.160
4.
Fireworks Display
at Marina Bay

00:07:21.670 --> 00:07:23.440
What's with the getup?

00:07:23.440 --> 00:07:24.840
The answer to that is simple.

00:07:24.840 --> 00:07:24.880
1. Singing the national anthem

00:07:24.840 --> 00:07:24.880
2. Celebrating the Lunar New Year

00:07:24.840 --> 00:07:24.880
3. Flying the national flag

00:07:24.840 --> 00:07:24.880
4. The fireworks display at Marina Bay

00:07:24.840 --> 00:07:27.130
Isn't it number 3,
"flying the national flag"?

00:07:27.130 --> 00:07:29.090
After all, there's a "rope" that goes up "a pole".

00:07:29.110 --> 00:07:31.070
Wow!
That's correct!

00:07:31.070 --> 00:07:32.640
Should've expected
as much from you.

00:07:32.640 --> 00:07:34.640
Alright then,
here's one more question!

00:07:34.640 --> 00:07:35.350
No, that's enough.

00:07:35.350 --> 00:07:35.840
What?

00:07:37.910 --> 00:07:41.140
It really is lonesome
when the kids aren't here...

00:07:49.900 --> 00:07:51.900
Man...
Damn you, Haibara.

00:08:17.530 --> 00:08:18.300
Ran...?

00:08:18.300 --> 00:08:19.870
Ah, Ran-neechan.

00:08:19.870 --> 00:08:24.120
What are you... doing... here...?

00:08:25.330 --> 00:08:28.020
Ran...-neechan...?

00:08:28.020 --> 00:08:31.530
I've been waiting <i>forever</i> for you.

00:08:37.390 --> 00:08:39.200
H-Huh?

00:08:39.200 --> 00:08:40.910
What is this place?!

00:08:40.680 --> 00:08:42.620
It's so big!

00:08:42.060 --> 00:08:43.380
Is that Ran's voice?

00:08:43.380 --> 00:08:44.760
Where in the world am I...?

00:08:44.760 --> 00:08:46.570
Am I locked up in something?!

00:08:46.580 --> 00:08:47.590
Damn it!

00:08:47.590 --> 00:08:50.920
Oh?
There, now I can...

00:08:55.860 --> 00:08:56.720
Whoa!

00:08:58.280 --> 00:08:59.890
Huh?

00:09:01.580 --> 00:09:02.680
What?

00:09:07.380 --> 00:09:11.610
The... Merlion...?

00:09:17.800 --> 00:09:19.620
What?!

00:09:19.620 --> 00:09:23.370
I'm in Singapore?!

00:09:36.760 --> 00:09:36.800
PRESENTED BY KIENAI

00:09:36.760 --> 00:09:36.800
DETECTIVE CONAN

00:09:43.970 --> 00:09:46.580
I'm high school detective, Kudo Shinichi.

00:09:44.890 --> 00:09:46.100
Kudo Shinichi

00:09:46.580 --> 00:09:50.320
While visiting an amusement park with my childhood friend and classmate, Mouri Ran...

00:09:50.320 --> 00:09:54.020
I witnessed a man in black in the midst of a suspicious transaction.

00:09:55.900 --> 00:09:58.160
While caught up in watching the deal...

00:09:58.160 --> 00:10:01.740
I failed to notice his
partner sneaking up behind me.

00:10:04.450 --> 00:10:07.410
That man forced me to take poison...

00:10:07.410 --> 00:10:08.700
And when I came to...

00:10:12.150 --> 00:10:14.070
My body had shrunk.

00:10:16.340 --> 00:10:18.930
If those guys found out that
Kudo Shinichi was still alive...

00:10:18.930 --> 00:10:22.380
They'd come after me again, and put those around me at risk.

00:10:23.180 --> 00:10:26.170
At Professor Agasa's suggestion,
I decided to hide my true identity.

00:10:26.170 --> 00:10:29.150
And the moment
Ran asked for my name...

00:10:29.150 --> 00:10:31.150
I became Edogawa Conan.

00:10:30.350 --> 00:10:32.820
Edogawa Conan

00:10:31.150 --> 00:10:33.020
In order to obtain
information on those guys...

00:10:33.020 --> 00:10:36.650
I went to live with Ran,
whose father is a private detective.

00:10:38.630 --> 00:10:41.550
As such, one of my
strongest rivals is this man:

00:10:41.550 --> 00:10:43.260
Kaito Kid.

00:10:43.260 --> 00:10:46.720
He's a phantom thief whose true identity remains unknown, a master of disguise...

00:10:46.720 --> 00:10:49.980
And a cunning man who,
somehow, knows who I really am.

00:10:49.980 --> 00:10:52.520
One of these days, I'm going
to catch him with my own two hands!

00:10:52.520 --> 00:10:55.360
Kid's rival is Kyogoku Makoto.

00:10:55.360 --> 00:10:56.860
Despite only being
a high school student...

00:10:56.860 --> 00:10:59.530
He's a karate master who
boasts a 400-match win streak.

00:10:59.530 --> 00:11:03.400
And for some reason, it seems
he's madly in love with Suzuki Sonoko...

00:11:03.400 --> 00:11:05.160
Ran's classmate and daughter
of the Suzuki Financial Group.

00:11:05.160 --> 00:11:06.420
What are you looking at?!

00:11:06.420 --> 00:11:08.620
Hurry up and say
that thing you always do.

00:11:09.940 --> 00:11:11.850
Even though I've shrunk,
my mind remains the same...

00:11:11.850 --> 00:11:13.980
That of an unbeaten great detective.

00:11:14.920 --> 00:11:19.450
There's always only one truth!

00:11:25.050 --> 00:11:27.470
What happened to my hand...?

00:11:27.470 --> 00:11:29.680
And I don't have any
of the professor's gadgets!

00:11:29.680 --> 00:11:32.270
I know!
I'm sure Ran was here!

00:11:33.540 --> 00:11:36.050
Wait for me, Ran-neechan!

00:11:37.690 --> 00:11:39.970
Oh, Shinichi!
We're over here!

00:11:39.970 --> 00:11:40.650
What?!

00:11:40.650 --> 00:11:43.840
Sorry I kept you waiting.

00:11:43.840 --> 00:11:46.760
Where did you go?!
We've been looking all over for you.

00:11:46.760 --> 00:11:50.270
The old man was saying it's hot,
so I was guiding him over to a shady tree.

00:11:50.270 --> 00:11:53.000
Wow, thanks!

00:11:53.000 --> 00:11:55.930
Oh... Your dad just
never changes, does he?

00:11:55.930 --> 00:11:56.770
Hey, Ran!

00:11:56.770 --> 00:11:58.780
Can you go buy me some water?!

00:11:58.780 --> 00:12:00.620
Guess I'll have to...

00:12:00.620 --> 00:12:03.220
Hey, let's go together!

00:12:03.220 --> 00:12:04.090
Come on, hurry!

00:12:04.090 --> 00:12:05.530
A-Alright...

00:12:05.530 --> 00:12:09.180
My, they've sure got some
good vibes going on between them.

00:12:10.040 --> 00:12:12.040
That bastard...

00:12:15.340 --> 00:12:16.620
I feel so revived now!

00:12:16.620 --> 00:12:17.230
Oh?

00:12:17.230 --> 00:12:19.300
What's that dangling
from your neck, Dad?

00:12:19.300 --> 00:12:20.130
Huh?

00:12:20.130 --> 00:12:23.220
I have my passport inside of this.

00:12:23.220 --> 00:12:25.160
That way, I won't lose it
or have it stolen.

00:12:25.160 --> 00:12:26.400
Good idea, don't you think?

00:12:26.400 --> 00:12:27.600
Oh come on, Dad.

00:12:27.600 --> 00:12:30.310
You don't need to do that,
because Singapore is completely safe.

00:12:30.310 --> 00:12:31.890
Like hell it is!

00:12:30.310 --> 00:12:32.040
Hey.
So you've woken up?

00:12:32.040 --> 00:12:33.600
I knew it was you!

00:12:34.600 --> 00:12:37.560
Wait, how did you
get out of the suitcase?

00:12:37.560 --> 00:12:38.770
With this.

00:12:38.770 --> 00:12:41.170
When I jammed it
with the tip of this pen...

00:12:41.170 --> 00:12:44.280
It opened surprisingly easily,
even from the inside.

00:12:44.280 --> 00:12:46.220
I thought a simple ballpoint pen
wouldn't be a problem...

00:12:46.220 --> 00:12:48.660
But with you,
I guess I can't be too careful!

00:12:48.660 --> 00:12:51.370
That's what I should
be saying to you, Kaito Kid!

00:12:53.410 --> 00:12:54.800
Ah, there it is.

00:12:55.670 --> 00:12:58.120
More importantly,
what's the big idea?!

00:12:58.120 --> 00:13:01.670
Heh... The answer's
right there in front of you.

00:13:01.670 --> 00:13:03.030
W-What?

00:13:06.090 --> 00:13:07.820
Isn't that Sonoko's...?

00:13:07.820 --> 00:13:10.100
At the end of the 19th century...

00:13:10.100 --> 00:13:14.770
A pirate ship sank just off the coast of Singapore,
while thought to have been carrying...

00:13:14.770 --> 00:13:17.400
A legendary hidden treasure.

00:13:17.400 --> 00:13:19.970
It was the world's
finest quality blue sapphire...

00:13:19.970 --> 00:13:24.700
Also known as the
"Fist of Blue Sapphire".

00:13:25.610 --> 00:13:37.370
World Watch

00:13:25.610 --> 00:13:37.370
Pirate Ship's Treasure
Recovered in Singapore

00:13:25.610 --> 00:13:28.870
Please be careful of the strobing
lights from the camera's flashes.

00:13:25.610 --> 00:13:37.370
Weather Forecast

00:13:25.610 --> 00:13:37.370
Train Service
Status

00:13:25.610 --> 00:13:37.370
Due to a person
entering onto
the train tracks
at Shibahama
Station on the
Touto Loop Line,
train service has
been delayed.

00:13:25.610 --> 00:13:30.050
It's a big jewel that
Mr. Zhonhan Chen successfully salvaged last year.

00:13:29.200 --> 00:13:33.250
Tonight's Weather

00:13:30.050 --> 00:13:31.720
Now that you mention Zhonhan Chen...

00:13:30.410 --> 00:13:37.370
"An Authority in Singapore's Financial World"
Mr. Zhonhan Chen

00:13:31.720 --> 00:13:34.160
He's one of Singapore's most influential people.

00:13:34.180 --> 00:13:34.910
That's right.

00:13:34.910 --> 00:13:37.370
And this old guy sure loves martial arts.

00:13:37.370 --> 00:13:39.810
He embedded the jewel
in the champion belt...

00:13:39.810 --> 00:13:43.230
And decided to host
a karate tournament.

00:13:43.230 --> 00:13:46.630
And the winner gets
the legendary jewel, huh?

00:13:46.630 --> 00:13:48.660
That sure is a pastime for the rich.

00:13:48.660 --> 00:13:50.010
Exactly.

00:13:50.010 --> 00:13:54.750
So I had thought I could just take the jewel in the bustle of the tournament...

00:13:54.750 --> 00:13:57.960
But I couldn't possibly enter
the country as Kid, now could I?

00:13:57.960 --> 00:14:00.400
If you're only after the jewel...

00:14:00.400 --> 00:14:02.980
You didn't need
to bring me along with you!

00:14:03.880 --> 00:14:06.490
This is a bit of a special case.

00:14:06.490 --> 00:14:09.240
Well, I'll explain the situation
to you gradually as we go along.

00:14:09.240 --> 00:14:10.430
Why, you...!

00:14:10.430 --> 00:14:11.410
What's that?!

00:14:12.310 --> 00:14:13.990
Oh, Shinichi?

00:14:13.990 --> 00:14:15.640
Uh oh.
She's calling for me.

00:14:15.640 --> 00:14:16.580
Wait, Kid!

00:14:17.540 --> 00:14:20.290
If you do anything to Ran,
I'll make you pay the price for it!

00:14:20.290 --> 00:14:21.450
What...?

00:14:21.450 --> 00:14:24.480
S-Sorry, but I can't
guarantee you that I won't.

00:14:24.480 --> 00:14:27.450
Then I'll expose you for who
you really are right here, right now!

00:14:27.450 --> 00:14:28.930
You'd better not do that.

00:14:30.680 --> 00:14:35.180
You were only able to enter
the country because of this suitcase.

00:14:36.370 --> 00:14:40.040
It's specially equipped so that even the X-rays
in the baggage check can't pass through it.

00:14:40.040 --> 00:14:43.980
Inside of it, I put a portable
oxygen generator that lasts 12 hours.

00:14:43.980 --> 00:14:46.710
And so your body wouldn't start hurting
even after being in there for so long...

00:14:46.710 --> 00:14:50.300
I made sure it's a top-class product packed
with the highest-quality cushioning.

00:14:50.300 --> 00:14:54.450
I'm sure you get what I mean.
Don't you, "great detective"?

00:14:54.450 --> 00:14:56.270
If you don't have my help...

00:14:56.270 --> 00:14:59.350
You won't be able to leave this country, since you don't have a passport.

00:14:59.350 --> 00:15:01.710
Meaning you won't
be able to go back to Japan.

00:15:02.690 --> 00:15:04.520
There you are, Shinichi!

00:15:04.520 --> 00:15:07.710
Sheesh. I look away for a second,
and you've run off somewhere and disappeared...

00:15:08.690 --> 00:15:09.720
Oh?

00:15:12.330 --> 00:15:14.430
I-Isn't that the twerp?!

00:15:14.430 --> 00:15:16.450
How did you get here?

00:15:16.450 --> 00:15:17.770
Conan-kun?

00:15:17.770 --> 00:15:19.620
Ah, he ran away!

00:15:19.620 --> 00:15:21.850
He sure surprises you, doesn't he?

00:15:21.850 --> 00:15:24.090
He's apparently
a child from around here.

00:15:24.090 --> 00:15:25.690
What?! He is?!

00:15:25.690 --> 00:15:28.400
Even so, this kid looks
so much like him...

00:15:25.690 --> 00:15:28.400
You two let yourselves
be fooled way too easily!

00:15:25.690 --> 00:15:28.400
You two let yourselves
be fooled way too easily!

00:15:28.400 --> 00:15:29.320
Little boy...

00:15:29.320 --> 00:15:30.750
What's your name?

00:15:30.750 --> 00:15:33.570
Wait, do you know Japanese?

00:15:34.050 --> 00:15:35.830
Um...

00:15:36.930 --> 00:15:37.830
This boy's...

00:15:39.120 --> 00:15:39.160
Edogawa Ranpo's   Complete Works

00:15:39.120 --> 00:15:39.160
Conan Doyle Selected Best

00:15:39.370 --> 00:15:39.460
Edogawa Ranpo's   Complete Works

00:15:39.370 --> 00:15:39.460
Conan Doyle Selected Best

00:15:41.440 --> 00:15:42.540
Arthur!

00:15:42.540 --> 00:15:44.960
My name is Arthur Hirai!

00:15:44.960 --> 00:15:47.020
Arthur Hirai?

00:15:47.020 --> 00:15:49.880
My mom is Japanese, so...

00:15:49.900 --> 00:15:51.720
I'm Suzuki Sonoko.

00:15:51.720 --> 00:15:53.570
I'm Mouri Ran.

00:15:53.570 --> 00:15:59.430
And over there is my dad,
Mouri Kogoro.

00:15:59.430 --> 00:16:00.870
Nice to meet you.

00:16:00.870 --> 00:16:02.870
Y-Yeah...
Nice to meet you, too.

00:16:02.870 --> 00:16:05.960
Sorry, Ran.
I have to leave for a little while.

00:16:05.960 --> 00:16:07.070
Oh, okay.

00:16:08.150 --> 00:16:09.130
Hey, little boy...

00:16:09.130 --> 00:16:10.540
Where are your mom and dad?

00:16:10.540 --> 00:16:14.200
Uh, um...
They're traveling in Japan.

00:16:14.200 --> 00:16:15.170
What?!

00:16:15.170 --> 00:16:17.560
And they left you at home
all by yourself, Arthur-kun?

00:16:17.560 --> 00:16:20.180
Yeah, but it's okay.
I'm used to it.

00:16:20.180 --> 00:16:21.210
I see...

00:16:21.210 --> 00:16:23.710
In that case, do you
want to come along with us?

00:16:23.710 --> 00:16:25.000
Can I?

00:16:25.000 --> 00:16:26.750
Yeah, of course you can.

00:16:28.570 --> 00:16:29.600
Oh, right!

00:16:29.600 --> 00:16:31.170
I'm going to go look
and see how Dad's doing.

00:16:31.860 --> 00:16:33.430
S-Sure.

00:16:33.430 --> 00:16:36.220
At any rate, he sure is late.

00:16:36.220 --> 00:16:38.200
He could have at least texted me.

00:16:38.200 --> 00:16:41.430
And I'm sure we were
supposed to meet up here, too...

00:16:42.440 --> 00:16:43.690
Move it!
You're all in the way!

00:16:43.690 --> 00:16:45.440
Out of the way!

00:16:45.440 --> 00:16:47.440
What the hell're you looking at?!

00:16:47.440 --> 00:16:49.050
Who're those guys?

00:16:49.050 --> 00:16:51.960
The man in the
center is Nakatomi Reijiro.

00:16:51.960 --> 00:16:53.420
Nakatomi...

00:16:53.420 --> 00:16:56.200
Oh, the president
of Nakatomi Shipping.

00:16:56.200 --> 00:16:57.760
He's known for being
a shrewd, talented man...

00:16:56.660 --> 00:16:59.740
Nakatomi Reijiro (39)
President of Nakatomi Shipping

00:16:57.760 --> 00:17:00.200
But there are some dark rumors
about him that never stop.

00:17:01.120 --> 00:17:04.810
Hey, babe.
Did you come to Singapore all alone?

00:17:04.810 --> 00:17:06.500
If you'd like, how
about coming with me—

00:17:06.500 --> 00:17:08.170
I don't have time
for this right now.

00:17:08.170 --> 00:17:09.290
Go away!

00:17:10.360 --> 00:17:12.400
Are you really okay
with saying that to me?

00:17:12.400 --> 00:17:16.840
If I felt like it, shoving a lone girl
like you into my car would be a cinch.

00:17:14.840 --> 00:17:16.840
New Message

00:17:14.840 --> 00:17:16.840
To:

00:17:14.840 --> 00:17:16.840
Subject:

00:17:14.840 --> 00:17:16.840
I guess you haven't been able to come yet?

00:17:14.840 --> 00:17:16.840
I'm waiting for you in front of the Merlion!

00:17:14.840 --> 00:17:16.840
ABC

00:17:14.840 --> 00:17:16.840
Emoji

00:17:14.840 --> 00:17:16.840
Stickers

00:17:17.700 --> 00:17:18.700
Sonoko!

00:17:19.600 --> 00:17:21.160
Shinichi?!

00:17:21.160 --> 00:17:23.230
Don't interfere.

00:17:23.230 --> 00:17:23.730
Huh?

00:17:24.600 --> 00:17:25.870
Hey!

00:17:38.720 --> 00:17:41.790
She's with me.
What business do you have with her?

00:17:41.790 --> 00:17:43.600
W-Who the hell are you?!

00:17:43.600 --> 00:17:45.790
Makoto-san! You need
to at least check your messages!

00:17:45.790 --> 00:17:48.830
I apologize.
I'm not very good with technology...

00:17:50.940 --> 00:17:52.130
Oww...!

00:17:52.940 --> 00:17:56.220
I'll get you for this!
I won't go so easy on you next time!

00:17:56.220 --> 00:17:59.280
Makoto-san!
I was so scared!

00:17:59.280 --> 00:18:01.660
I deeply apologize for being so late.

00:18:01.660 --> 00:18:03.700
You're so cool, Mister!

00:18:03.700 --> 00:18:06.890
I can do that, too!
Hiya! Hiya! Hiya!

00:18:06.890 --> 00:18:08.560
Hey, karate boy!

00:18:08.730 --> 00:18:10.190
How brave!

00:18:10.500 --> 00:18:11.790
Ah!

00:18:18.160 --> 00:18:20.070
Hey, come on!

00:18:20.070 --> 00:18:21.640
Are you okay, Sonoko?

00:18:21.640 --> 00:18:22.160
Oh?

00:18:22.160 --> 00:18:24.910
Yeah!
Because Makoto-san protected me!

00:18:24.910 --> 00:18:27.310
It's been quite a while, Kyogoku-san.

00:18:27.310 --> 00:18:28.810
Yes, it has.

00:18:28.810 --> 00:18:29.920
And who might you be?

00:18:29.920 --> 00:18:32.710
Nice to meet you.
I'm Kudo Shinichi.

00:18:32.710 --> 00:18:34.940
My name is Kyogoku Makoto.

00:18:40.660 --> 00:18:42.910
Makoto-san,
is something wrong?

00:18:42.910 --> 00:18:46.850
No, I just get the feeling this
isn't the first time I've met Kudo-kun.

00:18:49.210 --> 00:18:50.190
N—

00:18:50.190 --> 00:18:51.940
No, I'm sure you're
just imagining things!

00:18:53.210 --> 00:18:56.490
Now, we've seen the Merlion,
so how about we start heading to the hotel?

00:18:56.490 --> 00:18:59.070
Oh, about that...

00:18:59.070 --> 00:19:00.200
Huh?

00:19:02.640 --> 00:19:05.330
You can't participate
in the tournament anymore?!

00:19:05.330 --> 00:19:08.330
We came all this way
to see your match, too...

00:19:08.330 --> 00:19:10.050
I do apologize.

00:19:10.050 --> 00:19:15.340
I had accepted a certain someone's invitation
and entered into today's tournament...

00:19:15.340 --> 00:19:17.050
In other words, a sponsor?

00:19:17.050 --> 00:19:17.590
Yes.

00:19:17.590 --> 00:19:21.410
Sherilyn Tan, a woman
who works as an attorney...

00:19:21.410 --> 00:19:24.910
Asked if I would participate, saying she would cover all my travel and lodging expenses.

00:19:24.910 --> 00:19:28.060
But she suddenly passed away.

00:19:29.180 --> 00:19:31.750
And today,
someone connected with her...

00:19:31.750 --> 00:19:34.630
Told me to act like she had
never talked to me about anything.

00:19:34.630 --> 00:19:35.940
No way!

00:19:35.940 --> 00:19:41.360
Those who are said to be the strongest martial artists in Singapore will be participating in this tournament.

00:19:41.360 --> 00:19:44.370
They are opponents I really wanted
to try fighting against, even just once...

00:19:44.370 --> 00:19:45.890
All right!

00:19:45.890 --> 00:19:48.580
I'll be your sponsor!

00:19:48.580 --> 00:19:49.310
What?!

00:19:49.310 --> 00:19:51.330
Just leave it to me!

00:19:51.330 --> 00:19:55.500
That's the daughter of the
Suzuki Financial Group for you.

00:19:55.500 --> 00:19:55.880
Uncle Jirokichi

00:19:55.500 --> 00:19:55.750
Call in Progress

00:19:55.500 --> 00:19:55.540
The Call Has Ended

00:19:57.340 --> 00:19:59.130
Everything's been taken care of!

00:19:59.130 --> 00:20:02.660
Makoto-san, I was able to get you
reentered as an invited competitor!

00:20:02.660 --> 00:20:04.330
Really, Sonoko-san?!

00:20:04.330 --> 00:20:05.460
Yeah!

00:20:06.740 --> 00:20:09.640
And I had them make
Makoto-san's hotel the same as ours.

00:20:09.640 --> 00:20:11.440
So it's a double date!

00:20:13.120 --> 00:20:14.650
It is, isn't it?

00:20:14.650 --> 00:20:17.650
If you've talked and settled everything, how about we head back to the hotel, huh?

00:20:17.650 --> 00:20:20.010
I wanna hurry and chug some beers!

00:20:20.010 --> 00:20:21.400
Mouri-san!

00:20:22.010 --> 00:20:24.720
Would you be Mouri Kogoro-san?

00:20:24.720 --> 00:20:26.160
Huh? Yes...

00:20:26.160 --> 00:20:29.420
My name is Rishi, a reserve officer.

00:20:29.420 --> 00:20:30.830
It's an honor to meet you.

00:20:30.830 --> 00:20:33.080
Uh-huh...
Same to you.

00:20:33.080 --> 00:20:36.770
Um...
A reserve officer?

00:20:36.770 --> 00:20:37.340
That's right!

00:20:37.340 --> 00:20:40.410
As a specialist in
criminal behavior psychology...

00:20:40.410 --> 00:20:43.610
I've received special permission
to assist with investigations.

00:20:43.610 --> 00:20:45.110
Oh, is that so?

00:20:45.110 --> 00:20:46.090
Actually...

00:20:46.090 --> 00:20:50.350
I had been waiting here for you since
I heard you had entered the country, Mouri-san.

00:20:50.350 --> 00:20:51.910
You were waiting for me?

00:20:51.910 --> 00:20:55.250
Yes, because most tourists come here.

00:20:55.250 --> 00:20:58.000
B-But why me?

00:20:58.000 --> 00:21:02.110
There's actually a case I want
your help with, Detective Mouri.

00:21:02.110 --> 00:21:02.860
Huh?

00:21:02.860 --> 00:21:04.320
No way!

00:21:04.320 --> 00:21:06.160
I'm in the middle
of my vacation right now!

00:21:06.160 --> 00:21:06.890
Hey, hold up.

00:21:06.890 --> 00:21:10.010
I think it'd be better
to go along with him here.

00:21:10.010 --> 00:21:11.500
What? Why?

00:21:11.500 --> 00:21:14.830
If you get along well
with a reserve officer...

00:21:14.830 --> 00:21:17.750
You might be able to have him show you
some really good, cheap places to go.

00:21:17.750 --> 00:21:21.000
Maybe even the casinos...
You catch my drift, right?

00:21:21.000 --> 00:21:22.820
Uh, well...

00:21:22.820 --> 00:21:25.090
You might just be right.

00:21:26.600 --> 00:21:27.730
Very well!

00:21:27.730 --> 00:21:31.140
I, the great detective Mouri Kogoro,
will make a special exception and assist you!

00:21:31.140 --> 00:21:33.140
Oh, brother...

00:21:31.140 --> 00:21:33.140
What an honor!

00:21:33.140 --> 00:21:36.420
Detective Mouri, you're a hero
to my father's home country of Japan...

00:21:36.420 --> 00:21:38.150
And I'm a huge fan of yours, too!

00:21:39.380 --> 00:21:43.320
This actually arrived
at the home of a certain businessman.

00:21:44.630 --> 00:21:46.200
Wow!

00:21:46.200 --> 00:21:49.620
Advance Notice

00:21:46.200 --> 00:21:49.620
I shall come to have the legendary
treasure rest in my fist:
the sapphire, protected by the lion,
that emits a lucid, brilliant azure.

00:21:46.200 --> 00:21:49.620
Kaito Kid

00:21:46.200 --> 00:21:49.300
Kaito Kid!
Kaito Kid-sama!

00:21:51.280 --> 00:21:54.120
Leon's Residence

00:21:54.200 --> 00:21:57.540
I received a report that the Suzuki Group became the sponsor...

00:21:57.540 --> 00:21:58.790
...for Kyogoku.

00:21:58.790 --> 00:22:00.420
Can you beat him?

00:22:00.420 --> 00:22:01.960
There is no need for concern.

00:22:01.960 --> 00:22:03.510
No matter who...

00:22:02.210 --> 00:22:05.220
Hezli Jamaluddin (25)
Leon's Head of Security

00:22:03.510 --> 00:22:05.970
I will put him down in one blow.

00:22:05.970 --> 00:22:07.430
Good to know.

00:22:08.590 --> 00:22:09.640
Come in.

00:22:09.800 --> 00:22:10.970
Excuse me.

00:22:11.390 --> 00:22:14.140
Mr. Ramanathan has arrived with someone...

00:22:11.470 --> 00:22:14.470
Rachel Cheung (29)
Leon's Secretary

00:22:14.140 --> 00:22:15.480
...he'd like to introduce.

00:22:15.640 --> 00:22:16.940
He's early.

00:22:16.940 --> 00:22:19.190
Please bring him in to the lounge.

00:22:19.190 --> 00:22:20.610
Understood.

00:22:21.770 --> 00:22:23.860
So, how about Kid?

00:22:24.070 --> 00:22:26.990
Apologies. We are still investigating.

00:22:27.450 --> 00:22:29.490
Along with Sherilyn Tan...

00:22:29.490 --> 00:22:32.660
There are issues with handling information.

00:22:32.660 --> 00:22:34.870
I have a hunch who was behind it.

00:22:34.870 --> 00:22:36.750
You take care of it, then.

00:22:36.750 --> 00:22:39.210
Whoa!
This is incredible!

00:22:39.210 --> 00:22:41.130
Settle down, Dad!

00:22:41.130 --> 00:22:42.980
Oh! Even this suit of armor...

00:22:42.980 --> 00:22:44.800
Is so arm-azing!

00:22:47.360 --> 00:22:47.720
Whoa!

00:22:49.130 --> 00:22:49.850
What?

00:22:50.740 --> 00:22:51.780
Are you okay?

00:22:51.780 --> 00:22:52.890
Y-Yeah...

00:22:52.890 --> 00:22:55.970
Dad!
Get it together.

00:22:55.970 --> 00:22:59.060
I'm sorry.
I'm sorry about my dad.

00:22:58.040 --> 00:23:01.330
So who exactly is Leon Lowe?

00:23:01.330 --> 00:23:05.460
Leon-sensei was originally a noted criminal behavior psychologist...

00:23:05.460 --> 00:23:09.490
Who arrested countless heinous killers
by cooperating with the police.

00:23:09.490 --> 00:23:10.570
Wow...

00:23:10.570 --> 00:23:13.580
So basically, he's the
great detective of Singapore?

00:23:13.580 --> 00:23:15.890
He left the police force two years ago...

00:23:15.890 --> 00:23:20.080
And is currently having much success
as the president of a security company.

00:23:20.080 --> 00:23:24.500
I had also studied criminal behavior
psychology from Leon-sensei.

00:23:24.500 --> 00:23:25.840
Oh, I see.

00:23:25.840 --> 00:23:28.610
So the advance notice
came to this Leon guy?

00:23:28.610 --> 00:23:31.090
No, I'll explain everything in order.

00:23:31.090 --> 00:23:33.090
First, please look at this.

00:23:33.090 --> 00:23:37.950
Kaito Kid is after a jewel
called the "Fist of Blue Sapphire".

00:23:37.950 --> 00:23:40.770
It belongs to Mr. Zhonhan Chen,
a businessman.

00:23:40.770 --> 00:23:44.130
Kid's advance notice came to him.

00:23:44.130 --> 00:23:48.010
In that case, shouldn't we go
to this Zhonhan-Whatever guy's place...?

00:23:48.010 --> 00:23:52.410
The jewel is actually being stored
underground, beneath this estate.

00:23:52.410 --> 00:23:54.660
The jewel's here?

00:23:54.660 --> 00:23:57.770
Yes.
That is the wish of its owner.

00:23:57.770 --> 00:24:01.480
The safes here use an independently developed,
state-of-the-art security system...

00:24:01.480 --> 00:24:02.920
Making them even safer
than a bank vault...

00:24:02.920 --> 00:24:04.770
State-of-the-art, huh?

00:24:04.770 --> 00:24:08.300
Sounds like even that darn Kid
will have a lot of trouble this time around.

00:24:08.300 --> 00:24:10.130
You sure are one to talk.

00:24:10.130 --> 00:24:11.420
What are you talking about?!

00:24:11.420 --> 00:24:13.760
No matter how
state-of-the-art the safe is...

00:24:13.760 --> 00:24:16.140
It'll be child's play
when it comes to Kid-sama!

00:24:16.140 --> 00:24:17.160
Hey, Sonoko...

00:24:17.160 --> 00:24:21.890
Don't you know about Kid-sama's
magnificent stealing techniques, Ran?

00:24:21.890 --> 00:24:26.020
He could even steal the hearts
of every woman around the world—

00:24:26.020 --> 00:24:27.630
Stop, Sonoko!

00:24:27.630 --> 00:24:28.650
Huh?

00:24:30.630 --> 00:24:31.280
Ah!

00:24:32.490 --> 00:24:33.030
Well...

00:24:33.030 --> 00:24:35.700
Well...
Except for me and Ran, that is.

00:24:35.700 --> 00:24:36.870
Isn't that right, Ran?!

00:24:36.870 --> 00:24:38.540
Y-Yes, of course.

00:24:43.770 --> 00:24:46.310
You're not gonna
go unscathed if you're careless.

00:24:46.310 --> 00:24:48.320
Oh, <i>give me a break</i>...

00:24:49.150 --> 00:24:51.070
What a lovely inner garden!

00:24:51.070 --> 00:24:52.440
It's okay.

00:24:52.440 --> 00:24:54.180
It's a pleasure to meet all of you.

00:24:54.180 --> 00:24:56.550
My name is Leon Lowe.

00:24:56.550 --> 00:25:01.140
And this man is my bodyguard and head of security, Hezli Jamaluddin.

00:25:01.140 --> 00:25:03.460
Please allow him to join us.

00:25:08.770 --> 00:25:10.230
Mr. Kyogoku.

00:25:11.110 --> 00:25:13.110
I was hoping to see you.

00:25:13.400 --> 00:25:14.360
Thank you.

00:25:14.360 --> 00:25:15.990
I do karate, too.

00:25:15.990 --> 00:25:18.990
I always wanted to have a match with you.

00:25:19.580 --> 00:25:22.090
I have my own gym in this match.

00:25:20.140 --> 00:25:20.990
Oh!

00:25:20.990 --> 00:25:23.980
So you're the famous detective,
Mouri Kogoro-san?

00:25:22.090 --> 00:25:24.770
Can we train together tonight?

00:25:23.980 --> 00:25:26.420
Oh, why thank you.

00:25:24.770 --> 00:25:28.290
Sounds great.
Please let me join you.

00:25:26.420 --> 00:25:30.500
I never expected to have so many people
in a foreign country know my name.

00:25:31.150 --> 00:25:32.230
It's weird.

00:25:33.030 --> 00:25:34.860
I don't feel anything.

00:25:34.860 --> 00:25:36.340
What is it?

00:25:40.510 --> 00:25:41.770
No way.

00:25:41.770 --> 00:25:45.270
And you're the high school
detective, Kudo Shinichi-san.

00:25:45.270 --> 00:25:46.660
Nice to meet you.

00:25:47.270 --> 00:25:50.690
It seems you're more
of a magician than a detective.

00:25:50.690 --> 00:25:51.570
Wha—?!

00:25:52.460 --> 00:25:54.070
I can tell by your fingers.

00:25:54.070 --> 00:25:55.970
They're slender and supple.

00:25:55.970 --> 00:25:59.010
I'm a detective nonetheless,
so rather than physical strength...

00:25:59.010 --> 00:26:01.080
I prefer challenges
that get my gears up here turning.

00:26:01.560 --> 00:26:02.990
I see.

00:26:02.990 --> 00:26:07.870
Oh, and I take it the young woman
over there is Suzuki Sonoko-san?

00:26:07.870 --> 00:26:10.630
We can't let our guard
down around this guy.

00:26:10.940 --> 00:26:13.130
You can't come in! Please wait!

00:26:13.280 --> 00:26:15.530
That's okay. Don't bother.

00:26:15.530 --> 00:26:18.130
Oh!
Mouri Kogoro-sensei!

00:26:18.130 --> 00:26:21.160
My wife and I are huge fans of yours!

00:26:18.590 --> 00:26:21.680
Zhonhan Chen (70)
Authority in Singapore's
Financial World

00:26:21.160 --> 00:26:22.390
R-Right.

00:26:22.390 --> 00:26:24.640
Can I take a photo with you?

00:26:24.640 --> 00:26:26.890
A-A "photo"?
Oh, you mean a picture!

00:26:25.020 --> 00:26:27.980
Sorry. He came in all of a sudden...

00:26:26.890 --> 00:26:29.150
Okay, okay!
I'd be happy to!

00:26:27.980 --> 00:26:29.100
It's all right.

00:26:29.100 --> 00:26:32.820
I would like to show everyone our safe room.

00:26:32.820 --> 00:26:33.610
That's good!

00:26:33.610 --> 00:26:35.610
I'd love to come along!

00:26:35.610 --> 00:26:39.990
And by all means, I'd love to have you see
the Fist of Blue Sapphire up close.

00:26:41.640 --> 00:26:45.790
Beyond this door is the safe room,
my very own pride and joy.

00:26:45.790 --> 00:26:50.290
This can only be opened
by a select few individuals.

00:27:04.860 --> 00:27:07.740
The surface of the walls
are made of heat-resistant metal alloys...

00:27:07.740 --> 00:27:09.270
So absolutely
no one can destroy them.

00:27:09.270 --> 00:27:09.980
What?!

00:27:09.850 --> 00:27:13.270
Plus, everything is completely
sealed off from the outside.

00:27:10.850 --> 00:27:12.610
Sorry, sorry! Nothing!

00:27:13.270 --> 00:27:16.380
And it's setup so that each piece of cargo
is periodically moved to a different location.

00:27:16.380 --> 00:27:19.220
This safe is specially made,
packed with my own concepts...

00:27:19.220 --> 00:27:22.510
Meaning it's the only one of
its kind anywhere in the world.

00:27:23.870 --> 00:27:25.350
W-What's going on?!

00:27:25.350 --> 00:27:28.410
Everyone, please step back a bit.

00:27:30.480 --> 00:27:35.800
This jewel is called the "Fist of Blue Sapphire",
and is said to be the emblem of the king of all pirates.

00:27:36.300 --> 00:27:38.880
It's a huge cultural treasure.

00:27:37.300 --> 00:27:38.890
Can you see it, Arthur-kun?

00:27:38.890 --> 00:27:40.800
Yep! Thanks!

00:27:40.800 --> 00:27:42.080
I see.

00:27:42.080 --> 00:27:46.310
As long as it's here, I'm sure
even Kid can't meddle with it.

00:27:46.310 --> 00:27:48.870
Things won't work out that way.

00:27:48.870 --> 00:27:51.140
While the karate tournament
that starts tomorrow is being held...

00:27:51.140 --> 00:27:53.900
It's been decided that the belt
will be on display at the stadium.

00:27:53.900 --> 00:27:56.770
In other words, during
the time of the tournament...

00:27:56.770 --> 00:27:59.780
It will be kept safely
in one room of the stadium.

00:27:59.780 --> 00:28:03.570
It will be placed under strict security measures, but they're still lacking in comparison to here.

00:28:03.570 --> 00:28:04.140
I see.

00:28:04.200 --> 00:28:06.780
But there's also security for the stadium...

00:28:07.740 --> 00:28:10.790
Yes. We shall guard it at any cost!

00:28:12.540 --> 00:28:14.290
If anything happens to the Fist...

00:28:14.290 --> 00:28:18.550
You will be paying a hefty compensation fee.

00:28:19.260 --> 00:28:22.180
You said that the security measures
are lacking in comparison to here...

00:28:22.180 --> 00:28:27.310
But that means you believe Kid is waiting
until the sapphire is moved to the stadium, correct?

00:28:27.310 --> 00:28:28.510
Precisely.

00:28:28.510 --> 00:28:31.120
It would be far too risky
for him to come after it here.

00:28:31.120 --> 00:28:32.190
It sure would be.

00:28:32.190 --> 00:28:36.190
So while I can't do much, please allow me
to assist with guarding the jewel.

00:28:36.190 --> 00:28:38.690
Oh, thank you.

00:29:07.010 --> 00:29:08.180
This is a breeze!

00:29:10.330 --> 00:29:11.660
Whoa!

00:29:24.700 --> 00:29:26.740
Thanks for the fingerprints!

00:29:40.110 --> 00:29:41.840
Isn't this... <i>too </i>easy?

00:29:47.160 --> 00:29:48.260
I've been waiting for you.

00:29:51.080 --> 00:29:57.020
You making it all the way in here is just what I had expected from you, Kaito Kid.

00:29:57.020 --> 00:29:59.270
You sure are confident in yourself.

00:29:59.270 --> 00:30:03.860
I'm sorry, but I cannot afford
to have you take the jewel.

00:30:03.860 --> 00:30:06.930
Because I don't want to pay Zhonhan Chen
his compensation fee and such.

00:30:08.130 --> 00:30:11.720
Stealing treasures like that is my job.

00:30:11.720 --> 00:30:15.080
And the harder something is to steal...

00:30:15.080 --> 00:30:18.020
The more I get fired up!

00:30:29.430 --> 00:30:30.640
It's over.

00:30:37.730 --> 00:30:40.520
I hope you like the taste of Singaporean water.

00:31:01.980 --> 00:31:05.900
I never thought
he'd use a Taser on me!

00:31:39.540 --> 00:31:40.710
Kid!

00:31:43.940 --> 00:31:45.590
Is this seriously happening?!

00:31:47.000 --> 00:31:47.880
What the...?!

00:31:54.470 --> 00:31:55.430
What happened?

00:31:55.560 --> 00:31:56.540
It's Kid!

00:31:57.060 --> 00:31:59.430
Don't worry. I'm always...

00:32:01.540 --> 00:32:06.440
Those at the top always act
while considering the worst possible outcome!

00:32:06.440 --> 00:32:08.440
...one step ahead.

00:32:08.440 --> 00:32:11.200
I've gotta get out of here, and quickly!

00:32:20.750 --> 00:32:21.620
There he is!

00:32:45.500 --> 00:32:47.340
What a punch!

00:32:47.340 --> 00:32:49.650
I'd be in deep trouble
if I hadn't flown backwards!

00:32:49.650 --> 00:32:53.650
You're trespassing
on private property, aren't you?

00:32:53.650 --> 00:32:56.660
Wait, what are you doing here?

00:32:56.660 --> 00:33:00.290
I was invited to come here
if I wanted to do some training.

00:33:00.290 --> 00:33:02.960
I never would have expected
I could have a match with you here.

00:33:02.960 --> 00:33:04.920
No, no, no...
I don't want to have one!

00:33:04.920 --> 00:33:06.130
Don't waste your breath!

00:33:09.860 --> 00:33:11.090
Brace yourself for this!

00:33:29.590 --> 00:33:32.900
A soccer ball...?
Where in the world did it come from?

00:33:32.900 --> 00:33:35.360
Thanks, detective!

00:33:50.170 --> 00:33:51.920
This thing is awesome!

00:33:51.920 --> 00:33:54.020
Now I can fly freely,
even without wind.

00:33:54.020 --> 00:33:55.930
I've gotta be thankful for Jii-chan.

00:33:56.280 --> 00:33:57.930
But...

00:33:57.930 --> 00:34:00.350
Why would he go that far?

00:34:18.860 --> 00:34:20.220
You saved me back there!

00:34:20.220 --> 00:34:23.350
Looks like I was right
to return your equipment, just in case.

00:34:23.350 --> 00:34:25.580
It's not like I <i>wanted</i>
to save you, though.

00:34:26.580 --> 00:34:29.400
More importantly,
isn't it about time you told me?!

00:34:29.400 --> 00:34:31.880
What's the real reason
you brought me here?!

00:34:34.320 --> 00:34:35.380
Whoa!

00:34:38.180 --> 00:34:42.740
Leon had been searching
for the Fist of Blue Sapphire for years.

00:34:42.740 --> 00:34:45.080
But when he was just
one step away from recovering it...

00:34:45.080 --> 00:34:48.190
Zhonhan Chen beat him to it.

00:34:48.190 --> 00:34:52.900
Apparently, someone leaked
the location of the sunken ship to him.

00:34:53.690 --> 00:34:56.940
The most suspicious one is Sherilyn Tan.

00:34:56.940 --> 00:35:00.220
She had worked as a legal advisor
for Leon's firm for some time...

00:35:00.220 --> 00:35:02.700
But the relationship
between the two soured.

00:35:02.700 --> 00:35:06.330
According to rumor, the reason
she became Kyogoku's sponsor...

00:35:06.330 --> 00:35:08.700
To hinder Jamaluddin's victory.

00:35:08.700 --> 00:35:12.340
Basically, she wanted to
obstruct Leon from obtaining the jewel.

00:35:12.340 --> 00:35:14.360
If that's true...

00:35:14.360 --> 00:35:19.070
Then the rumors that the location of the
sunken ship was leaked also have a ring of truth to them.

00:35:19.070 --> 00:35:21.840
And then Sherilyn Tan was killed.

00:35:21.840 --> 00:35:24.660
If we assume the rumors
about the leak are true...

00:35:24.660 --> 00:35:28.000
That would mean Leon
had a motive to kill Sherilyn.

00:35:28.000 --> 00:35:30.600
What do the police think?

00:35:30.600 --> 00:35:34.360
Unfortunately, Leon was
removed from the suspect list.

00:35:34.360 --> 00:35:35.650
Why?

00:35:35.650 --> 00:35:38.760
Because there's
a much more likely suspect!

00:35:38.760 --> 00:35:40.630
A suspect?!

00:35:43.410 --> 00:35:45.830
The police haven't made this public...

00:35:45.830 --> 00:35:50.410
But a card was left at
the scene of Sherilyn Tan's murder.

00:35:50.410 --> 00:35:52.290
An advance notice from me.

00:35:53.020 --> 00:35:55.010
So that's it.

00:35:55.010 --> 00:35:55.800
But...

00:35:55.800 --> 00:35:59.800
Why do I have to see such amazing scenery with this guy, of all people?!

00:35:59.800 --> 00:36:03.660
If I'm going to see it with someone,
I wish it was with...

00:36:12.560 --> 00:36:15.750
It's time for you to go back
to being Arthur Hirai.

00:36:15.750 --> 00:36:19.070
By the way, I'm sure Arthur is
from Sir Arthur Conan Doyle...

00:36:19.070 --> 00:36:20.800
But what's this "Hirai"?

00:36:20.800 --> 00:36:22.450
Oh, well...

00:36:22.450 --> 00:36:26.260
I got it from Edogawa Ranpo's
real name, Hirai Taro.

00:36:22.700 --> 00:36:22.740
Edogawa Ranpo
(Pen Name)

00:36:24.410 --> 00:36:25.660
Hirai    Taro
(Real Name)

00:36:25.910 --> 00:36:26.410
Sir Arthur Conan Doyle

00:36:26.260 --> 00:36:27.700
Oh, I get it.

00:36:27.700 --> 00:36:31.000
But more importantly,
this is clearly a trap!

00:36:31.000 --> 00:36:33.060
I know.

00:36:33.060 --> 00:36:36.860
That's why I brought
you along, <i>great detective</i>.

00:36:36.860 --> 00:36:39.000
Aren't you good
with this kind of thing?

00:36:39.000 --> 00:36:43.010
I understand your reasons now,
though I don't like how you went about doing it.

00:36:43.700 --> 00:36:45.730
I, Kid-sama...

00:36:46.430 --> 00:36:50.520
Can't just keep quiet
about this, now can I?

00:36:56.170 --> 00:36:59.900
You sure were slow.
I've been waiting for you all this time.

00:36:59.900 --> 00:37:01.880
Sorry, sorry.

00:37:01.880 --> 00:37:03.650
Hey, look at this.

00:37:03.650 --> 00:37:06.430
This nightscape is so beautiful.

00:37:06.430 --> 00:37:08.660
Don't you think it's romantic?

00:37:12.480 --> 00:37:13.620
Wha—?

00:37:16.980 --> 00:37:19.070
Don't be so bashful.

00:37:19.070 --> 00:37:21.480
The two of us are dating, aren't we?

00:37:21.480 --> 00:37:22.630
Y-Yeah...

00:37:22.630 --> 00:37:24.630
What?! You are?!

00:37:24.630 --> 00:37:26.640
Damn it...

00:37:26.640 --> 00:37:29.950
Hasn't Ran even
realized he's a fake?!

00:37:29.950 --> 00:37:32.930
Oh, but if she <i>did</i> realize that,
I wouldn't be able to go back to Japan...!

00:37:38.230 --> 00:37:41.030
Raffles Hotel

00:37:49.050 --> 00:37:52.310
When it comes to Singapore,
it's gotta be the Singapore Sling!

00:37:52.310 --> 00:37:53.540
Gimme another glass!

00:37:54.330 --> 00:37:55.200
Mouri-san?

00:37:55.200 --> 00:37:55.890
Huh?

00:37:55.890 --> 00:37:59.060
A-And you are...?

00:37:59.060 --> 00:38:01.670
Do you mind if I sit here?

00:38:02.670 --> 00:38:06.680
N-N-Not at all, not at all.
Let's drink together.

00:38:07.450 --> 00:38:09.140
Actually, I...

00:38:09.140 --> 00:38:10.180
Oh?

00:38:11.050 --> 00:38:12.180
Ah!

00:38:12.700 --> 00:38:13.680
Uh-oh...

00:38:13.680 --> 00:38:16.440
This is terrible!
What have I done?!

00:38:17.210 --> 00:38:19.330
I'm so sorry!

00:38:19.330 --> 00:38:22.110
No, no... It's fine.
Don't worry about it.

00:38:24.110 --> 00:38:26.450
Mr. Mouri... A call for you.

00:38:26.450 --> 00:38:28.340
Huh? "Call"?

00:38:28.340 --> 00:38:31.010
It seems there's a
phone call for you, Mouri-san.

00:38:31.010 --> 00:38:32.430
For me?

00:38:32.430 --> 00:38:33.970
Who could it be?

00:38:33.970 --> 00:38:35.320
Mouri-san.

00:38:35.320 --> 00:38:36.120
Oh?

00:38:36.560 --> 00:38:38.870
There's something I really
want to talk with you about!

00:38:40.060 --> 00:38:41.730
Come here tomorrow!

00:38:41.730 --> 00:38:43.320
Huh?!

00:38:44.770 --> 00:38:45.880
Jeez...

00:38:47.610 --> 00:38:48.380
Huh...

00:38:49.730 --> 00:38:51.390
What the...?!
They hung up on me!

00:38:51.390 --> 00:38:55.220
Time to start drinking again!

00:39:00.980 --> 00:39:04.020
Singapore Indoor Stadium

00:39:04.020 --> 00:39:06.380
Who do you think will win?

00:39:06.380 --> 00:39:07.840
Mr. Kyogoku!

00:39:07.840 --> 00:39:09.320
Because he's never lost!

00:39:09.320 --> 00:39:12.550
Wow, he hasn't?
That's the first I've heard about that.

00:39:12.550 --> 00:39:16.540
So his considerable effort done
with proper positioning and direction...

00:39:16.540 --> 00:39:18.480
Must really be bearing fruit.

00:39:18.480 --> 00:39:20.440
Did you two understand that?

00:39:20.440 --> 00:39:21.790
Yep!

00:39:30.860 --> 00:39:34.030
Who will get
the Fist of Blue Sapphire?

00:39:51.570 --> 00:39:52.700
That was so fast!

00:39:52.700 --> 00:39:55.950
This Jamaluddin guy
seems ridiculously strong.

00:39:55.950 --> 00:40:00.520
He has both speed and technique combined with heavyweight-class power.

00:40:00.520 --> 00:40:01.710
He seems to be
quite a formidable foe.

00:40:02.730 --> 00:40:05.380
I expected as much from the
captain of the Teitan High karate club!

00:40:05.380 --> 00:40:08.070
You notice things
that most people wouldn't.

00:40:08.070 --> 00:40:09.450
Hey...

00:40:09.450 --> 00:40:12.410
If the jewel goes to Kyogoku-san...

00:40:12.410 --> 00:40:14.600
Doesn't that mean you
won't be able to get to it anymore?

00:40:14.600 --> 00:40:16.420
Right.

00:40:16.420 --> 00:40:19.140
Because I want to be
around him as little as possible.

00:40:21.890 --> 00:40:24.750
Ah, Makoto-san's here!

00:40:26.250 --> 00:40:27.900
Come on!
You all cheer him on, too!

00:40:27.900 --> 00:40:31.010
Wait, why'd you bring
the twerp here with you?

00:40:31.010 --> 00:40:33.410
He's gotten pretty attached
to me, for some reason.

00:40:43.730 --> 00:40:45.190
Bow to each other!

00:40:49.030 --> 00:40:50.190
Oh?

00:40:50.280 --> 00:40:51.530
Begin!

00:41:01.200 --> 00:41:02.390
That's just scary...

00:41:01.740 --> 00:41:02.330
Way to go!

00:41:02.330 --> 00:41:04.160
You're so cool,
Makoto-san!

00:41:04.160 --> 00:41:06.920
Oh, how I want to
go see him right now!

00:41:06.920 --> 00:41:07.560
Oh?

00:41:07.560 --> 00:41:07.610
Incoming Call
Dad

00:41:07.560 --> 00:41:07.610
Submenu

00:41:07.560 --> 00:41:07.610
Contact List

00:41:07.560 --> 00:41:07.610
Add to Contacts

00:41:07.560 --> 00:41:07.610
Turn Mute ON

00:41:07.560 --> 00:41:09.800
It's from Dad.

00:41:09.820 --> 00:41:12.840
Like I've been telling you,
I am not anyone suspicious!

00:41:12.840 --> 00:41:14.430
Dad!

00:41:14.430 --> 00:41:16.050
What happened?

00:41:16.050 --> 00:41:19.240
Ran!
Please explain to these guys for me!

00:41:19.240 --> 00:41:22.000
I've pulled out everything
I have that's made of metal.

00:41:22.000 --> 00:41:24.060
But even so...

00:41:25.420 --> 00:41:26.540
No entry!

00:41:26.540 --> 00:41:27.750
Aren't I fine now?!

00:41:27.750 --> 00:41:28.500
No!

00:41:28.500 --> 00:41:32.260
Damn it!
I'll never be able to get in at this rate!

00:41:32.260 --> 00:41:34.630
Mouri-san,
is everything okay?!

00:41:34.630 --> 00:41:35.510
Ah, Rishi-san!

00:41:35.510 --> 00:41:38.350
He's a staff member. Please let him in.

00:41:38.640 --> 00:41:39.640
Yes, sir.

00:41:39.660 --> 00:41:41.040
Thank you, Mr. Rishi!

00:41:41.040 --> 00:41:42.770
I'm glad I was able
to meet up with you.

00:41:42.770 --> 00:41:45.670
After the belt was unveiled
during the opening ceremony...

00:41:45.670 --> 00:41:48.420
It's now being stored
in an underground safe.

00:41:48.420 --> 00:41:50.770
If you'd like,
I could show you to it later.

00:41:50.770 --> 00:41:53.400
But all things considered,
where have you been up until now?

00:41:53.400 --> 00:41:56.660
U-Uh, well...
I was doing some patrolling.

00:41:56.660 --> 00:41:59.660
Are you sure you didn't just
oversleep because of a hangover?

00:42:01.540 --> 00:42:04.680
The password
changes every ten minutes.

00:42:04.680 --> 00:42:08.540
It's controlled by a computer,
which informs us via email.

00:42:08.540 --> 00:42:11.520
The only ones who get this
are Inspector Aidan and myself...

00:42:11.520 --> 00:42:15.650
As well as Leon-sensei, who manages
the safe, making a total of three.

00:42:18.180 --> 00:42:20.850
Wow, this room has nothing in it.

00:42:20.850 --> 00:42:22.180
Not at all.

00:42:22.180 --> 00:42:25.680
There's weight sensors in the floor,
and security cameras in the ceiling...

00:42:25.680 --> 00:42:28.940
And then there's officers stationed
all around the stadium, surrounding it.

00:42:28.940 --> 00:42:33.340
Oh! With this, I'm sure even
that phantom thief can't do a thing.

00:42:33.340 --> 00:42:35.690
Mouri-san,
smoking is forbidden here.

00:42:35.690 --> 00:42:37.610
Ah, sorry about that.

00:42:37.610 --> 00:42:38.490
Huh?

00:42:38.490 --> 00:42:40.240
Rachel Cheong

00:42:41.990 --> 00:42:45.100
I was so hammered,
I completely forgot about this.

00:42:45.100 --> 00:42:48.620
She handed me this at the bar last night,
saying she needed to talk about something.

00:42:48.620 --> 00:42:52.880
Rachel Cheong

00:42:50.440 --> 00:42:52.880
That's the business
card of Leon's secretary.

00:42:52.880 --> 00:42:55.070
What?! It is?

00:42:55.070 --> 00:42:58.150
To tell you the truth,
I was drunk and don't really remember.

00:42:58.150 --> 00:42:59.780
How did you know?

00:42:59.780 --> 00:43:02.490
The mark of Leon-san's company is on it.

00:43:02.490 --> 00:43:03.970
Oh...
Its mark, huh?

00:43:04.830 --> 00:43:05.950
"3 PM."

00:43:05.950 --> 00:43:09.790
"Meet me at the back
of National Stadium gate 3."

00:43:09.790 --> 00:43:11.460
That's what written here.

00:43:11.460 --> 00:43:14.360
Oh...
It also says, "Tell no one."

00:43:14.360 --> 00:43:18.380
I see.
So it's at 3 PM, huh?

00:43:18.380 --> 00:43:19.990
It's almost 3!

00:43:19.990 --> 00:43:21.930
M-Mouri-san!

00:43:21.930 --> 00:43:24.580
Making a lady wait
is shameful for a man!

00:43:39.320 --> 00:43:41.340
That was truly a fine match.

00:43:41.340 --> 00:43:45.790
I'll start looking forward
to tomorrow's semifinals.

00:43:45.790 --> 00:43:47.620
Thank you very much.

00:43:47.620 --> 00:43:49.600
Your strength is extraordinary.

00:43:49.600 --> 00:43:51.250
So how about it?

00:43:51.250 --> 00:43:53.110
Do you have any desire
to be my bodyguard?

00:43:55.110 --> 00:43:56.480
Please excuse me.

00:44:01.010 --> 00:44:02.510
Now, wait a minute.

00:44:02.510 --> 00:44:04.370
I was just joking now, of course!

00:44:04.370 --> 00:44:07.490
But there actually
is one thing I want to ask you.

00:44:08.870 --> 00:44:09.750
So tell me...

00:44:11.290 --> 00:44:15.040
For what reason
do you have your fist?

00:44:15.040 --> 00:44:19.860
There's something out there
for which you pursue strength.

00:44:19.860 --> 00:44:22.890
What is it, exactly,
that spurs you onward?

00:44:25.050 --> 00:44:27.370
So you can't answer?

00:44:27.370 --> 00:44:30.680
An imperfect fist that
has no purpose is dangerous.

00:44:30.680 --> 00:44:32.790
Not only to yourself...

00:44:32.790 --> 00:44:35.690
But it will lead the people around you
to misfortune and unhappiness.

00:44:35.690 --> 00:44:38.090
The people around me?
Misfortune and unhappiness?

00:44:38.090 --> 00:44:39.290
Yes.

00:44:39.290 --> 00:44:42.130
Like the person
you love, for example.

00:44:42.130 --> 00:44:44.930
Even you have
someone like that, don't you?

00:44:45.890 --> 00:44:50.810
Your fist is dangerous,
and it may hurt the person you love.

00:44:50.810 --> 00:44:54.810
And what will
you do if that happens?

00:44:58.880 --> 00:45:01.590
I'm looking forward
to tomorrow's match.

00:45:13.410 --> 00:45:14.460
Do you still need something?

00:45:17.330 --> 00:45:18.360
Good job out there.

00:45:18.360 --> 00:45:20.110
Sonoko-san.

00:45:20.110 --> 00:45:20.940
Oh, you...

00:45:20.940 --> 00:45:23.340
You just wouldn't come,
so we came to see you.

00:45:23.340 --> 00:45:25.360
I apologize for making you wait.

00:45:25.360 --> 00:45:27.890
So let's all go get some lunch!

00:45:27.890 --> 00:45:29.950
There's this place
I really want to go...

00:45:29.950 --> 00:45:31.060
Sorry, Sonoko.

00:45:31.060 --> 00:45:33.020
You two can go eat without me.

00:45:33.020 --> 00:45:34.370
What? Why?

00:45:34.370 --> 00:45:36.270
I'm really sorry!

00:45:36.270 --> 00:45:40.380
But since Shinichi's guarding the jewel,
it doesn't look like he can get away from here.

00:45:40.380 --> 00:45:42.110
I see...

00:45:42.110 --> 00:45:44.610
Then I guess there's
nothing you can do about that.

00:45:44.610 --> 00:45:47.070
How about the
two of us go, Makoto-san?

00:45:47.070 --> 00:45:48.070
Okay.

00:45:48.070 --> 00:45:49.970
See you later, Ran.

00:45:49.970 --> 00:45:51.890
Please excuse us
for leaving ahead of you.

00:45:51.890 --> 00:45:54.330
I want you to eat
a lot now, Makoto-san!

00:45:54.330 --> 00:45:55.840
Thank you so much.

00:46:07.340 --> 00:46:10.330
Now, be alert and look everywhere!

00:46:10.330 --> 00:46:14.000
If you see anything unusual, report it.

00:46:14.000 --> 00:46:15.500
And act immediately!

00:46:16.000 --> 00:46:16.710
And...

00:46:18.670 --> 00:46:20.000
Are you okay?

00:46:20.250 --> 00:46:21.880
I'm so sorry.

00:46:22.130 --> 00:46:23.760
I'm sorry, too.

00:46:32.720 --> 00:46:34.310
Inspector Aidan!

00:46:35.230 --> 00:46:38.150
Sorry, I couldn't help but notice.

00:46:38.400 --> 00:46:40.520
I-I'm sorry... What...?

00:46:40.900 --> 00:46:42.270
There you go!

00:46:42.570 --> 00:46:44.610
Keep up the good work.

00:46:45.070 --> 00:46:46.030
Yes, ma'am!

00:46:47.780 --> 00:46:49.990
Everything okay with the safe?

00:46:50.280 --> 00:46:52.330
Yes, sir. Everything is alright.

00:46:52.530 --> 00:46:54.660
Excuse me! I'm so sorry.

00:46:54.660 --> 00:46:55.410
What's the matter?

00:46:55.410 --> 00:46:58.870
Inspector Aidan is calling you to come quick!

00:46:59.170 --> 00:47:00.330
B-But...

00:47:00.580 --> 00:47:02.130
I'll look after this place.

00:47:02.460 --> 00:47:03.420
O-Okay.

00:47:03.590 --> 00:47:05.710
We'll be back soon. Thank you.

00:47:10.280 --> 00:47:11.530
Now...

00:47:14.200 --> 00:47:16.370
I'll be taking the treasure!

00:47:35.480 --> 00:47:37.220
I'll be taking this!

00:47:39.640 --> 00:47:41.980
Huh? Did this get
caught on something?

00:47:41.980 --> 00:47:42.750
Wha—?

00:47:49.360 --> 00:47:51.340
A dead body?!
And even worse...

00:47:52.820 --> 00:47:54.850
It's Rachel's?!

00:47:54.850 --> 00:47:55.980
This is bad!

00:47:55.980 --> 00:47:57.470
I've gotta get out of here, and quick!

00:48:00.250 --> 00:48:01.480
Oh?

00:48:01.480 --> 00:48:03.440
Are those some type of letters?

00:48:05.250 --> 00:48:06.460
Crap!

00:48:11.990 --> 00:48:13.120
Stop right there!

00:48:18.290 --> 00:48:19.620
Drop the gun, now!

00:48:20.120 --> 00:48:22.000
Kid, you're under arrest!

00:48:25.880 --> 00:48:26.380
What?

00:48:31.780 --> 00:48:32.670
Honestly...

00:48:32.670 --> 00:48:35.390
How long is Rachel-san
going to make us wait?

00:48:35.390 --> 00:48:38.040
Let's wait ten more minutes— Huh?

00:48:38.040 --> 00:48:39.830
W-What's going on?!

00:48:39.830 --> 00:48:41.830
It might be Kid!

00:48:41.830 --> 00:48:43.060
Hey, wait!

00:48:46.860 --> 00:48:48.020
He's here!

00:48:48.340 --> 00:48:51.050
Whoa!
This is really bad!

00:48:51.050 --> 00:48:54.030
But I'll have this in the bag
if I can get out of the grounds!

00:49:01.660 --> 00:49:03.830
There were <i>this</i> many of them?!

00:49:13.110 --> 00:49:14.340
Hey, wait!

00:49:19.100 --> 00:49:19.760
Damn!

00:49:20.060 --> 00:49:22.850
Go! Arrest him at any cost!

00:49:22.850 --> 00:49:23.770
Yes, sir!

00:49:24.330 --> 00:49:26.540
Oh, come on...
Is it really okay to let him leave?

00:49:26.540 --> 00:49:29.270
There you are, Mouri-san!
I've been looking for you!

00:49:29.270 --> 00:49:32.300
Man, this sure turned
into a huge problem.

00:49:32.300 --> 00:49:35.260
Who would have thought Kid
would appear in broad daylight like this?

00:49:35.260 --> 00:49:37.390
But rest assured.

00:49:37.390 --> 00:49:40.200
I, the great detective Mouri Kogoro,
will immediately begin tracking him down—

00:49:40.200 --> 00:49:41.770
This isn't the time for that!

00:49:41.770 --> 00:49:44.140
Something terrible has happened!

00:49:44.140 --> 00:49:46.150
Please come to
the safe room right now!

00:49:46.150 --> 00:49:46.920
Huh?

00:49:50.050 --> 00:49:50.710
Look!

00:49:51.090 --> 00:49:53.720
There's a giant bird in the sky!

00:50:02.580 --> 00:50:04.330
Now that I've made it this far...

00:50:14.050 --> 00:50:15.970
W-What is this...?!

00:50:15.970 --> 00:50:19.090
The victim is Leon-sensei's
secretary, Rachel-san.

00:50:19.090 --> 00:50:20.580
Rachel-san?

00:50:22.180 --> 00:50:23.200
I see...

00:50:23.200 --> 00:50:25.350
Did you check the security cameras?

00:50:25.350 --> 00:50:26.330
They were no help.

00:50:26.330 --> 00:50:32.210
They were hacked so that a video showing
no one present would be sent over and over.

00:50:32.210 --> 00:50:34.860
So, have you marked
someone as the killer?

00:50:34.860 --> 00:50:36.610
Of course we have.

00:50:36.610 --> 00:50:39.070
And we're currently pursuing him
to the best of our ability.

00:50:39.070 --> 00:50:41.850
"Currently pursuing him?"
You don't mean...

00:50:41.850 --> 00:50:45.160
Make no mistake.
Kaito Kid is the killer!

00:50:45.160 --> 00:50:50.360
In any case, not disabling the alarm system
beforehand was a mistake on your part, Kid.

00:50:50.360 --> 00:50:51.480
Hey, you know...

00:50:51.480 --> 00:50:53.250
If that was true, then at the time...

00:50:53.250 --> 00:50:56.020
Shouldn't Rachel-san have
been coming to the stadium...

00:50:56.020 --> 00:50:58.030
For her appointment
with this nice man?

00:50:58.030 --> 00:51:00.260
Why was she in the safe room?

00:51:00.260 --> 00:51:02.490
Oh?
Come to think of it, that's true.

00:51:02.490 --> 00:51:05.220
According to the officers
who were in front of the safe room...

00:51:05.220 --> 00:51:08.520
It seems she came to tell them
that Inspector Aidan needed them.

00:51:08.520 --> 00:51:12.380
Perhaps it seemed urgent
and they prioritized that?

00:51:12.380 --> 00:51:15.230
After all, that big disturbance
happened right afterwards...

00:51:15.230 --> 00:51:18.940
But I've never heard
of Kid being a murderer.

00:51:20.990 --> 00:51:23.580
Ah, hey!
Don't just barge in!

00:51:23.580 --> 00:51:26.390
Jeez.
There he goes again!

00:51:28.330 --> 00:51:30.330
Hey, there's these
bloody letters here...

00:51:30.330 --> 00:51:31.340
Hey!

00:51:32.310 --> 00:51:34.110
Brats have to get out!

00:51:39.150 --> 00:51:40.510
Yeah.

00:51:40.510 --> 00:51:42.090
Take a look at this.

00:51:42.090 --> 00:51:43.140
I see.

00:51:44.180 --> 00:51:48.710
You've been completely set up,
haven't you, Kid?

00:51:52.900 --> 00:51:54.980
B-Bring it on.

00:51:54.980 --> 00:52:00.650
T-This has gotten...
pretty interesting, hasn't it...?

00:52:01.760 --> 00:52:04.830
Just as I would expect of something
you selected, Sonoko-san...

00:52:04.830 --> 00:52:08.330
Both the chicken rice and
watermelon juice were very delicious.

00:52:08.330 --> 00:52:09.640
I know, right?!

00:52:11.390 --> 00:52:13.150
Is there something else?

00:52:13.150 --> 00:52:17.420
W-Well, now that our stomachs are full...

00:52:17.420 --> 00:52:20.920
There is one place
I'd like to go, Makoto-san...

00:52:20.920 --> 00:52:22.660
I'll accompany you,
no matter where it is.

00:52:28.200 --> 00:52:29.790
This looks bad!

00:52:30.250 --> 00:52:31.330
Hey, girl!

00:52:31.330 --> 00:52:33.830
What are you going to do about this?

00:52:33.830 --> 00:52:36.630
Aren't you the
one who ran into <i>me</i>?!

00:52:36.630 --> 00:52:39.210
Huh? I don't know what you mean!

00:52:39.460 --> 00:52:40.510
C'mere!

00:52:47.470 --> 00:52:48.140
Shit!

00:52:56.520 --> 00:52:59.550
He may have
other companions lurking.

00:52:59.550 --> 00:53:02.550
Sonoko-san,
please keep close to me.

00:53:02.550 --> 00:53:03.910
O-Okay!

00:53:13.920 --> 00:53:18.960
Your fist is dangerous,
and it may hurt the person you love.

00:53:32.910 --> 00:53:34.330
Sonoko-san!

00:53:56.040 --> 00:53:57.560
I found it...

00:53:57.560 --> 00:53:59.090
Please help me!

00:54:28.140 --> 00:54:29.200
Sonoko-san!

00:54:31.030 --> 00:54:31.910
Is he alright?

00:54:31.910 --> 00:54:34.000
I'm calling for an ambulance.

00:54:34.000 --> 00:54:35.160
Is she a foreigner...?

00:54:37.690 --> 00:54:39.100
Sonoko-san!

00:54:46.950 --> 00:54:48.430
Sonoko-san.

00:54:48.430 --> 00:54:50.120
Sonoko-san!

00:54:50.740 --> 00:54:53.640
Sonoko-san! Sonoko-san!

00:55:02.540 --> 00:55:04.710
How did they say
her injuries are doing?

00:55:04.710 --> 00:55:07.130
He said they're
not life threatening.

00:55:07.130 --> 00:55:10.070
She's sleeping now, so they're going to admit her for the night...

00:55:10.070 --> 00:55:12.700
And then it seems
they'll examine her tomorrow.

00:55:13.280 --> 00:55:15.350
I'm so glad.

00:55:16.240 --> 00:55:19.020
But even so,
what a vicious hit and run...

00:55:19.020 --> 00:55:20.580
It's my fault.

00:55:20.580 --> 00:55:24.320
It's my fault that Sonoko-san...

00:55:26.110 --> 00:55:27.590
Sorry to have kept you waiting!

00:55:27.590 --> 00:55:29.740
My apologies for being late!

00:55:29.740 --> 00:55:31.340
No problem.
Good work out there.

00:55:31.340 --> 00:55:33.330
How's the investigation going?

00:55:33.330 --> 00:55:34.320
Yes, well...

00:55:34.320 --> 00:55:36.700
It took place in a back alley
where not many people pass through...

00:55:36.700 --> 00:55:38.370
So there aren't any witnesses.

00:55:38.370 --> 00:55:41.380
To be more accurate,
there were people there...

00:55:41.380 --> 00:55:46.110
But they were taken by surprise
when the patrol car was stolen, and fainted.

00:55:48.920 --> 00:55:49.720
Ah!

00:55:50.970 --> 00:55:52.740
I hope I haven't disturbed you.

00:55:52.740 --> 00:55:55.470
Leon-sensei?
What are you doing here?

00:55:55.470 --> 00:55:57.770
I heard about the accident
and flew over here.

00:55:57.770 --> 00:56:00.230
Sonoko's still sleeping...

00:56:00.230 --> 00:56:02.520
In that case, could I have
you give her these for me?

00:56:02.520 --> 00:56:03.880
Thank you.

00:56:07.780 --> 00:56:11.380
It seems my worry
was right on the mark.

00:56:11.380 --> 00:56:15.910
The god of fighting is testing you.

00:56:15.910 --> 00:56:21.640
He's saying that you do not yet have the
mind, body, and spirit required to wield your fist.

00:56:21.640 --> 00:56:25.060
I know.
I'll give you a charm.

00:56:26.630 --> 00:56:29.130
It's kind of like
a good luck charm bracelet.

00:56:29.130 --> 00:56:31.050
If this breaks...

00:56:31.050 --> 00:56:34.780
It's a sign of the god's acknowledgment that
you've come to have the proper mind, body, and spirit.

00:56:34.780 --> 00:56:38.470
But if you wield your fist
before this breaks...

00:56:38.470 --> 00:56:39.540
You know what
will happen, don't you?

00:56:44.920 --> 00:56:47.380
Oww...

00:56:48.420 --> 00:56:50.420
You took some
pretty heavy damage.

00:56:50.420 --> 00:56:52.740
A scratch like this is nothing.

00:56:52.740 --> 00:56:53.420
Jeez...

00:56:53.420 --> 00:56:55.450
For them to come shooting
at me without restraint...

00:56:55.450 --> 00:56:58.060
I was really outwitted this time.

00:56:58.060 --> 00:57:02.060
They're making Rachel-san's
murder out to be your doing.

00:57:02.060 --> 00:57:06.940
It's all a trap intended
to frame you for the crimes.

00:57:06.940 --> 00:57:09.180
It's almost like magic.

00:57:09.180 --> 00:57:11.570
Even though I'm not there...

00:57:11.570 --> 00:57:18.080
To the audience watching, I certainly appear to be a murderer who may have been there.

00:57:18.080 --> 00:57:22.850
So basically, you can start to see how the trick is done if you change how you look at it?

00:57:24.710 --> 00:57:26.130
Yeah...

00:57:26.130 --> 00:57:31.300
A magician makes a person think as though there may be something in their clenched fist...

00:57:31.300 --> 00:57:36.660
And a detective correctly guesses what's in their fist before it opens, right?

00:57:44.960 --> 00:57:48.150
So correctly guess
what it is, great detective...

00:57:48.150 --> 00:57:53.280
The contents of the mysterious
clenched fist known as "murder".

00:57:53.800 --> 00:57:54.900
Jeez...

00:58:06.350 --> 00:58:07.420
Ah...

00:58:07.420 --> 00:58:09.920
Haven't you gone home yet, kid?

00:58:09.920 --> 00:58:12.990
Hey, can I spend the night
with you tonight?

00:58:12.990 --> 00:58:15.450
What...
At my house?

00:58:15.450 --> 00:58:18.680
I'd be all by myself,
even if I went home.

00:58:18.680 --> 00:58:22.830
And I'm scared from
all the stuff that just happened...

00:58:22.830 --> 00:58:24.750
But if I could tell them
I was with you, Rishi-san...

00:58:24.750 --> 00:58:27.690
I'm sure my mom and dad
would be relieved, too!

00:58:29.960 --> 00:58:34.360
After all, spending two consecutive nights in
the same room as that guy would be the worst.

00:58:40.990 --> 00:58:42.990
Oh, wow!

00:58:42.990 --> 00:58:46.230
Did you get all of these
from your dad, Rishi-san?

00:58:46.230 --> 00:58:47.500
That's right.

00:58:47.500 --> 00:58:49.150
You see, my father's an oceanographer.

00:58:49.150 --> 00:58:51.440
Sadly, he passed away five years ago...

00:58:51.440 --> 00:58:55.240
But over the course of his research,
he found fossils and such that had sank into the ocean.

00:58:55.240 --> 00:58:57.130
You're proud
of your dad, aren't you?

00:58:57.130 --> 00:58:58.490
Yeah!

00:58:58.490 --> 00:59:00.990
Well, I still have
some work left to do...

00:59:00.990 --> 00:59:02.890
So you go to sleep
ahead of me, Arthur-kun.

00:59:02.890 --> 00:59:04.750
Okay!

00:59:05.370 --> 00:59:07.270
Oh...
Hey, Rishi-san.

00:59:07.270 --> 00:59:10.380
What are the red marks on this map?

00:59:10.380 --> 00:59:14.400
Ah, they show the places
where ships were attacked by pirates.

00:59:14.400 --> 00:59:16.760
There are pirates, even nowadays?!

00:59:16.760 --> 00:59:17.920
There sure are!

00:59:17.920 --> 00:59:21.410
Long ago, there were lots
of them close to Singapore.

00:59:21.410 --> 00:59:26.660
But I'm more worried
about this murder case than pirates now.

00:59:26.660 --> 00:59:28.890
And then there's
Kaito Kid on top of it all.

00:59:28.890 --> 00:59:32.040
I borrowed some materials
from Assistant Inspector Aidan...

00:59:33.540 --> 00:59:36.110
But I guess I'll be
pulling an all-nighter tonight.

00:59:41.180 --> 00:59:43.490
I feel bad for
doing this to Rishi-san...

00:59:43.490 --> 00:59:45.310
But I'll have him get a good nap.

01:00:06.640 --> 01:00:08.960
Hey, what's that?

01:00:08.960 --> 01:00:10.710
I didn't know you
had something like that.

01:00:10.710 --> 01:00:12.850
Sonoko-san!
You came to?!

01:00:13.840 --> 01:00:15.610
Actually,
I did quite some time ago.

01:00:16.910 --> 01:00:19.150
I'm really so glad.

01:00:19.150 --> 01:00:21.590
Hey, is that some
kind of good luck charm?

01:00:21.590 --> 01:00:24.600
Yeah...
It's something like that.

01:00:29.450 --> 01:00:31.520
No, you can't!
Please take it easy and rest.

01:00:33.380 --> 01:00:36.000
I'm not the least bit sleepy.

01:00:36.000 --> 01:00:39.030
This is so boring, even after
we came all the way to Singapore.

01:00:39.030 --> 01:00:41.090
It'll be bad for your body
if you try to do too much.

01:00:41.090 --> 01:00:42.910
So please take things
easy and rest tonight.

01:00:44.910 --> 01:00:47.470
You know, I've been wanting
to ask you this for a while...

01:00:47.470 --> 01:00:50.410
But why don't you ever take off
the band-aid by your left eyebrow?

01:00:50.410 --> 01:00:51.560
What?

01:00:51.560 --> 01:00:55.170
N-No...
This is nothing, really.

01:00:55.170 --> 01:00:57.040
Huh...?

01:01:14.520 --> 01:01:16.270
I thought we were not supposed to meet...

01:01:16.270 --> 01:01:18.230
...until everything was done?

01:01:18.480 --> 01:01:20.650
You bragged your plan was perfect...

01:01:20.650 --> 01:01:22.820
But are you totally sure?

01:01:23.820 --> 01:01:27.070
You look tough, but you're actually a coward.

01:01:27.330 --> 01:01:29.580
Now, watch your mouth...

01:01:38.590 --> 01:01:40.460
I always keep promises.

01:01:40.460 --> 01:01:41.590
I do.

01:01:47.700 --> 01:01:49.660
If you trick me,
I'll trick you back.

01:01:49.660 --> 01:01:52.020
That's how I roll.

01:02:04.800 --> 01:02:06.940
We have an announcement to make.

01:02:06.940 --> 01:02:08.550
In the second semifinals match...

01:02:08.530 --> 01:02:11.080
Makoto Kyogoku has withdrawn...

01:02:11.080 --> 01:02:13.870
And Tan Lee will proceed to the finals!

01:02:14.080 --> 01:02:14.620
Damn it!

01:02:15.210 --> 01:02:16.920
I didn't ask for this!

01:02:17.540 --> 01:02:19.540
You withdrew from the tournament?!

01:02:19.540 --> 01:02:21.820
Why?
Is it because of me?

01:02:21.820 --> 01:02:26.050
There's a chance that the gang who
attacked us could come to attack us again...

01:02:26.050 --> 01:02:28.930
So I couldn't possibly
leave your side, Sonoko-san.

01:02:29.800 --> 01:02:31.930
So it really is
because of me, isn't it?

01:02:31.930 --> 01:02:33.510
Go and be in the tournament!

01:02:33.510 --> 01:02:35.940
Isn't there an opponent
you want to fight against?!

01:02:35.940 --> 01:02:37.440
Yes.

01:02:37.440 --> 01:02:40.860
But since I couldn't even
protect you, Sonoko-san...

01:02:40.860 --> 01:02:43.710
It feels like I still lack something.

01:02:45.110 --> 01:02:47.280
You sure are
lacking in something.

01:02:47.280 --> 01:02:49.760
All you do is hide things
from me, Makoto-san!

01:02:49.760 --> 01:02:50.930
Hide things?

01:02:50.930 --> 01:02:55.290
You won't tell me about the bracelet or the band-aid, will you?

01:02:55.290 --> 01:02:58.920
No...
They're really, um...

01:02:59.790 --> 01:03:00.540
Get out.

01:03:00.540 --> 01:03:01.420
What?

01:03:01.420 --> 01:03:05.800
I don't want to be protected by a man who's full of lies like that!

01:03:08.240 --> 01:03:10.800
You know, I was
really worried yesterday.

01:03:10.800 --> 01:03:12.780
I could never get in touch with you.

01:03:12.780 --> 01:03:14.160
Sorry, sorry.

01:03:14.160 --> 01:03:16.960
I just got so absorbed
in chasing after Kid...

01:03:16.960 --> 01:03:19.060
But it's just what one would expect
of the magician under the moonlight.

01:03:19.060 --> 01:03:22.500
Catching him would be impossible even for me, Kudo Shinichi—

01:03:25.260 --> 01:03:26.720
Oh, Arthur-kun.

01:03:26.720 --> 01:03:27.950
Hello!

01:03:27.950 --> 01:03:31.320
Is your friend,
Sonoko-oneesan, okay?

01:03:31.320 --> 01:03:32.220
Yeah!

01:03:32.220 --> 01:03:34.120
I just dropped
by the hospital earlier...

01:03:34.120 --> 01:03:36.080
And the results of the examination
showed that there's no problems.

01:03:36.080 --> 01:03:39.350
It looks like she'll be released from the hospital
and go back to the hotel this afternoon.

01:03:39.350 --> 01:03:40.900
Wow, that's great.

01:03:40.900 --> 01:03:43.150
Thanks for worrying about her.

01:03:43.150 --> 01:03:45.110
Let's head back to the hotel soon.

01:03:45.110 --> 01:03:47.190
I'd like to consolidate
our luggage for going home.

01:03:47.190 --> 01:03:49.630
Are you okay with leaving
Sonoko-oneesan and her guy friend alone?

01:03:49.630 --> 01:03:50.590
Yeah...

01:03:50.590 --> 01:03:52.740
I thought I'd just
leave them be for a while.

01:03:52.740 --> 01:03:55.240
It looks like those two were
having some sort of disagreement...

01:03:55.240 --> 01:03:58.230
And Kyogoku-san even
withdrew from the tournament.

01:03:59.540 --> 01:04:02.150
Wait, Shinichi?

01:04:02.360 --> 01:04:04.900
Fountain of Wealth

01:04:04.900 --> 01:04:08.510
So, great detective, were you
able to gather anything last night?

01:04:08.510 --> 01:04:11.660
Based on the investigation reports
I saw at Rishi-san's house, it went like this...

01:04:16.720 --> 01:04:18.770
According to witness testimony...

01:04:18.770 --> 01:04:22.400
Sherilyn-san wasn't stabbed in the
shopping mall where she collapsed...

01:04:22.400 --> 01:04:25.670
But may have been
in the elevator of Tower 3.

01:04:25.670 --> 01:04:27.940
Why would someone go out of
their way to do it in the elevator?

01:04:27.940 --> 01:04:30.560
If things didn't work out,
they'd be no place to run to, would there?

01:04:34.180 --> 01:04:37.010
With a store-bought knife
still lodged in her back...

01:04:37.010 --> 01:04:38.850
She proceeded to move
to the shopping mall.

01:04:42.000 --> 01:04:43.440
And then immediately
after she collapsed...

01:04:43.440 --> 01:04:48.170
Her car exploded
in the underground parking garage...

01:04:48.170 --> 01:04:51.200
Resulting in a power outage
across the entire hotel.

01:04:51.200 --> 01:04:56.200
And so, the video feeds from
all the hotel security cameras were cut?

01:04:56.200 --> 01:04:59.370
What bothers me is that Leon
was at the scene of the crime.

01:04:59.370 --> 01:05:03.230
He had arranged a room for himself,
and another for Sherilyn-san.

01:05:03.230 --> 01:05:05.190
But when she was killed...

01:05:05.190 --> 01:05:08.780
A large number of witnesses saw
he had been riding a different elevator.

01:05:08.780 --> 01:05:10.610
So because his
alibi had been verified...

01:05:10.610 --> 01:05:13.430
He was excluded
from the line of investigation?

01:05:13.430 --> 01:05:14.610
Precisely.

01:05:14.610 --> 01:05:18.260
Come to think of it,
why did Leon have a suitcase?

01:05:18.260 --> 01:05:21.060
Ah, the police examined
the inside of it, of course...

01:05:21.060 --> 01:05:23.190
But it was empty.

01:05:23.190 --> 01:05:27.190
He had only sent the suitcase to
be repaired, and then came to pick it up.

01:05:27.190 --> 01:05:31.440
And it was verified that a store
near the hotel had received his request.

01:05:31.440 --> 01:05:33.780
So he has a perfect alibi, huh?

01:05:33.780 --> 01:05:34.990
There's one more thing...

01:05:34.990 --> 01:05:36.740
This.

01:05:36.740 --> 01:05:40.010
Why was this left behind
at the scene of the crime?

01:05:40.010 --> 01:05:42.180
Where was the need
to drag me into this?

01:05:42.180 --> 01:05:45.230
And it even went as far as to have clotted blood smeared on it.

01:05:45.230 --> 01:05:46.250
That being the case...

01:05:48.360 --> 01:05:51.940
They're an attempt to place
the crime of killing Rachel-san onto you.

01:05:51.940 --> 01:05:55.510
The knife used as the murder weapon was
the same as the one used when killing Sherilyn-san.

01:05:56.510 --> 01:06:01.290
Rachel-san had been put inside
the pedestal before I entered the safe room.

01:06:01.290 --> 01:06:03.080
But to enter the room...

01:06:03.080 --> 01:06:06.830
One has to get past the security officers and countless security systems.

01:06:06.830 --> 01:06:11.280
Someone who can slip past the eyes of the security and get in without touching the sensors...

01:06:12.230 --> 01:06:13.530
It's not me.

01:06:14.520 --> 01:06:17.160
Just as I thought,
Leon Lowe is the most suspicious.

01:06:17.160 --> 01:06:19.770
Leon, being the
manager of the safe room...

01:06:19.770 --> 01:06:22.180
Would be completely familiar
with the security systems in place.

01:06:22.180 --> 01:06:26.350
Furthermore, the belt had been
brought to the stadium yesterday morning.

01:06:26.350 --> 01:06:30.630
And Rachel-san has been confirmed
to have been alive up until two nights ago.

01:06:30.630 --> 01:06:35.300
In other words, it's very likely that the crime took place that night before the belt was moved.

01:06:36.260 --> 01:06:37.740
But for what reason?

01:06:37.740 --> 01:06:40.760
Why would he need
to kill his own secretary?

01:06:40.760 --> 01:06:43.430
Perhaps <i>that</i> could be his motive.

01:06:44.270 --> 01:06:48.270
Rachel-san had been trying
to tell the old man something.

01:06:45.270 --> 01:06:45.310
Rachel

01:06:48.270 --> 01:06:51.520
And those bloody letters
are a clue that she left behind.

01:06:51.520 --> 01:06:52.570
"She"...

01:06:52.570 --> 01:06:55.280
That refers to
another woman, but who?

01:06:52.820 --> 01:06:55.280
Another

01:06:52.820 --> 01:06:55.280
Woman

01:07:05.790 --> 01:07:07.480
It's no use.

01:07:07.480 --> 01:07:09.730
It feels like something
monumental is going to happen...

01:07:09.730 --> 01:07:11.420
But my thoughts just
won't come together.

01:07:11.420 --> 01:07:14.530
Even the great detective's
throwing his hands up?

01:07:14.530 --> 01:07:16.900
Then let's take a break
for the time being.

01:07:16.900 --> 01:07:18.860
Incidentally, there's something
in one of my fists, and—

01:07:18.860 --> 01:07:21.820
There's a coconut water in your left fist.

01:07:21.820 --> 01:07:23.060
That's correct!

01:07:23.060 --> 01:07:24.620
How'd you know?

01:07:24.620 --> 01:07:26.230
Weren't you just buying it?

01:07:26.230 --> 01:07:27.640
Ah, so you were watching me?

01:07:28.270 --> 01:07:29.900
Magic, huh?

01:07:30.650 --> 01:07:35.610
A magician makes a person think as though there may be something in their clenched fist...

01:07:35.610 --> 01:07:40.410
And a detective correctly guesses what's in their fist before it opens, right?

01:07:40.410 --> 01:07:42.930
Ah!
I've got it.

01:07:42.930 --> 01:07:47.870
Come to think of it, is Sonoko-ojousama
fighting with that one karate guy?

01:07:47.870 --> 01:07:48.910
That's what I heard.

01:07:48.910 --> 01:07:52.420
Well, I suppose getting caught in
a scuffle as well as a traffic accident...

01:07:52.420 --> 01:07:55.670
Would make one feel
pretty insecure and uneasy.

01:07:55.670 --> 01:07:57.310
So <i>that's</i> it.

01:07:57.310 --> 01:07:57.820
Huh?

01:07:57.820 --> 01:08:02.200
He caused Sonoko to get hurt,
and shook Makoto-san up emotionally.

01:08:02.200 --> 01:08:07.310
After all, Makoto-san is the
biggest obstacle to having Jamaluddin win.

01:08:07.310 --> 01:08:08.580
I get it.

01:08:08.580 --> 01:08:11.170
So you're saying that Leon
arranged to have that accident happen?

01:08:11.170 --> 01:08:14.290
And just as he planned,
Makoto-san withdrew from the tournament.

01:08:14.290 --> 01:08:17.590
And now Jamaluddin will most
certainly take the champion belt.

01:08:17.590 --> 01:08:21.200
In other words, it'll be passed into the hands of his employer, Leon.

01:08:21.200 --> 01:08:23.600
Along with the
Fist of Blue Sapphire.

01:08:23.600 --> 01:08:27.810
But why is Leon so fixated
on the Fist of Blue Sapphire?

01:08:27.810 --> 01:08:30.960
I've obtained something
that seems like it'd be a hint to that.

01:08:30.960 --> 01:08:33.730
This is a man Leon
had been meeting at dawn.

01:08:33.730 --> 01:08:35.880
Couldn't we determine
this man's identity?

01:08:35.880 --> 01:08:39.380
Well, it's not impossible...

01:08:39.380 --> 01:08:40.380
Tag, you're it!

01:08:39.380 --> 01:08:41.130
Now listen here, you!

01:08:41.130 --> 01:08:44.260
You suddenly called the professor and said that on second thought you'd go to Hokkaido, then hung up.

01:08:44.260 --> 01:08:45.910
So what are you doing right now?!

01:08:45.910 --> 01:08:48.330
Sorry, Haibara.
I've had a bunch of stuff to deal with here, too...

01:08:48.330 --> 01:08:50.580
Quiet down a little, you guys!

01:08:50.580 --> 01:08:51.750
Okay...

01:08:51.750 --> 01:08:52.870
Honestly.

01:08:52.870 --> 01:08:55.960
You're probably just wrapped up in a case somewhere, aren't you?

01:08:55.960 --> 01:08:57.440
Actually, that's exactly it.

01:08:57.440 --> 01:08:58.070
What?!

01:08:58.070 --> 01:09:01.630
I just sent you a data file
containing a picture that Kid took.

01:09:01.630 --> 01:09:04.320
Kid?!
You just said "Kid"...

01:09:04.320 --> 01:09:06.830
No way!
Kaito Kid showed up?!

01:09:06.830 --> 01:09:08.600
You're on the phone
with Conan-kun, correct?

01:09:08.600 --> 01:09:11.370
Conan-kun said he's
in Hokkaido right now?

01:09:11.370 --> 01:09:13.750
What would Kid want to steal there?

01:09:13.750 --> 01:09:15.440
A wood carving
of a bear or something?

01:09:15.440 --> 01:09:16.980
Maybe it's some Sapporo Ramen?

01:09:16.980 --> 01:09:18.980
He wouldn't steal something like that.

01:09:18.980 --> 01:09:20.260
Ai-chan!

01:09:20.260 --> 01:09:21.820
Please let me talk to him!

01:09:21.820 --> 01:09:22.630
Me too—

01:09:24.700 --> 01:09:27.200
Sorry.
The kids are over here to play right now...

01:09:27.200 --> 01:09:28.450
Ah, okay.

01:09:28.450 --> 01:09:30.540
I'll tell you all the
details after I've come back...

01:09:30.540 --> 01:09:34.210
But for now, I'd like you to look into
the identity of the man in that picture.

01:09:34.210 --> 01:09:36.170
Sure, sure. I got it.

01:09:36.170 --> 01:09:38.690
So, are you really alright?

01:09:38.690 --> 01:09:40.960
Yeah, somehow.

01:09:40.960 --> 01:09:43.340
I'm sure there's
no point in me telling you this...

01:09:43.340 --> 01:09:44.700
But don't do anything rash.

01:09:44.700 --> 01:09:46.050
Thank you.

01:09:46.960 --> 01:09:48.640
We'll be fine now.

01:09:48.640 --> 01:09:51.200
So, great detective,
what are you going to do now?

01:09:51.200 --> 01:09:53.330
I'm going to watch
and see how things play out.

01:09:53.330 --> 01:09:57.060
I'll see what moves Leon makes after
he's gotten his hands on the Fist of Blue Sapphire.

01:09:57.060 --> 01:09:58.710
But before that comes the old man.

01:09:59.360 --> 01:10:01.400
What...
Hey, wait!

01:10:06.280 --> 01:10:09.370
The winner of the Zhonhan Cup is...

01:10:09.970 --> 01:10:13.350
Jamaluddin!!!

01:10:19.150 --> 01:10:22.230
So, what do you think of my city plan?

01:10:25.280 --> 01:10:27.870
We cannot accept your proposal.

01:10:28.120 --> 01:10:28.740
Why?

01:10:28.870 --> 01:10:31.410
You lose nothing with this plan.

01:10:31.410 --> 01:10:33.580
It also benefits the country.

01:10:34.080 --> 01:10:35.620
It's too hasty.

01:10:35.620 --> 01:10:38.130
If you proceed with this much development...

01:10:38.130 --> 01:10:40.460
Some may be forced out of their homes.

01:10:40.630 --> 01:10:42.630
We can give them another place!

01:10:42.630 --> 01:10:44.470
My plan is perfect!

01:10:45.590 --> 01:10:47.430
You are too young.

01:10:47.430 --> 01:10:49.760
Learn some more, and come back.

01:10:56.730 --> 01:10:58.150
Old fool...

01:10:58.770 --> 01:11:01.520
Your era is now at an end.

01:11:02.230 --> 01:11:04.900
I will build a new city.

01:11:18.500 --> 01:11:19.630
Hands in the air!

01:11:20.630 --> 01:11:21.840
O-Okay, okay...

01:11:25.510 --> 01:11:28.010
You and I are very much
bound together by fate.

01:11:28.010 --> 01:11:32.510
Once this plan has succeeded,
we'll both be partners.

01:11:32.510 --> 01:11:34.290
I'm counting on you.

01:11:34.290 --> 01:11:36.560
I'm awfully indebted to you.

01:11:36.560 --> 01:11:41.020
I was suspected of theft, and it looked like the police were going to take me away...

01:11:41.020 --> 01:11:43.800
But it was you saving me
that started it all.

01:11:43.800 --> 01:11:46.780
And there's been so
many other times since then.

01:11:46.780 --> 01:11:50.760
It's because I knew you
were <i>the</i> Nakatomi Reijiro...

01:11:50.760 --> 01:11:55.040
Son of Nakatomi Juzo, who had been called the king of Japan's shipping industry.

01:11:55.040 --> 01:11:57.660
Don't mention my dad's name.

01:11:57.660 --> 01:12:00.080
Ah...
My apologies.

01:12:00.080 --> 01:12:03.940
At any rate,
everything will change tonight.

01:12:03.940 --> 01:12:07.050
How about we watch the moment
that happens from nearby?

01:12:09.510 --> 01:12:11.050
Come, let's go together...

01:12:11.050 --> 01:12:16.560
So we can be witnesses to the start
of what will go down in Singaporean history!

01:12:19.660 --> 01:12:20.560
Huh?

01:12:20.560 --> 01:12:21.850
Sorry about this, old man!

01:12:21.850 --> 01:12:22.440
What?

01:12:22.440 --> 01:12:24.440
W-What is this, all of a sudden?!

01:12:26.300 --> 01:12:27.690
No, stop it! You perv!

01:12:27.690 --> 01:12:29.440
Ah, this is it!

01:12:30.610 --> 01:12:30.650
TOMI

01:12:30.650 --> 01:12:30.780
NAKA

01:12:30.650 --> 01:12:30.780
TOMI

01:12:31.720 --> 01:12:33.030
Nakatomi?

01:12:33.030 --> 01:12:35.780
"Nakatomi",
as in Nakatomi Shipping?!

01:12:35.780 --> 01:12:37.290
Probably.

01:12:37.290 --> 01:12:39.870
I'll be borrowing this, old man!

01:12:42.210 --> 01:12:46.400
Did that brat
just call me old man?

01:12:48.040 --> 01:12:50.280
Why did you suddenly leave Japan?

01:12:50.280 --> 01:12:52.490
For a vacation.
A vacation.

01:12:52.490 --> 01:12:55.140
You also went to Singapore
five years ago, correct?

01:12:55.140 --> 01:12:59.770
Society

01:12:55.140 --> 01:12:59.770
Charging President Nakatomi
Regarding Suspicion of Bribing Politicians

01:12:55.140 --> 01:12:58.330
Yeah, and I've been there ever since.
What about it?!

01:12:57.850 --> 01:12:59.770
President of Nakatomi Shipping
Mr. Nakatomi Reijiro (39)

01:12:58.330 --> 01:12:59.770
Regarding President Nakatomi...

01:12:59.770 --> 01:13:01.910
So he's that guy
who was in the Merlion Plaza.

01:13:01.910 --> 01:13:04.750
Though he got taken out
by that karate guy.

01:13:07.340 --> 01:13:08.650
Oh, Haibara?

01:13:08.650 --> 01:13:11.010
Did you find out who that man is?

01:13:11.010 --> 01:13:12.910
Yeah...
I managed, somehow.

01:13:12.910 --> 01:13:16.910
Kudo Shinichi

01:13:12.910 --> 01:13:16.910
Singapore's Pirates

01:13:12.910 --> 01:13:14.870
His name is Eugene Lim.

01:13:14.870 --> 01:13:16.910
And shockingly, he's a pirate.

01:13:16.910 --> 01:13:17.760
A pirate?!

01:13:17.760 --> 01:13:21.230
There are recent eyewitness reports
regarding him in Singapore.

01:13:21.230 --> 01:13:23.920
I knew you could do it, Haibara.
I can really count on you.

01:13:23.920 --> 01:13:25.810
The fact that you're flattering me...

01:13:25.810 --> 01:13:28.480
Must mean you still have
something you want me to look into?

01:13:28.480 --> 01:13:29.900
Y-Yeah...

01:13:30.920 --> 01:13:34.080
Have you heard the name
Nakatomi Reijiro before?

01:13:34.080 --> 01:13:35.340
The one from Nakatomi Shipping.

01:13:35.340 --> 01:13:36.430
Yeah, I know it.

01:13:37.180 --> 01:13:40.870
I want to know the status of the ships
owned by the Nakatomi Shipping company.

01:13:40.870 --> 01:13:43.690
Just the ships in the area
around Singapore is fine.

01:13:46.690 --> 01:13:50.960
There are two cargo ships and
one oil tanker in the vicinity of Singapore.

01:13:50.960 --> 01:13:55.450
What I'm a little curious about is
that the oil tanker is deviating from its planned route.

01:13:55.450 --> 01:13:58.390
That's it!
Send me the data on that oil tanker!

01:13:58.390 --> 01:14:00.640
Okay.
I'll call you again.

01:14:00.640 --> 01:14:01.450
Yes, please.

01:14:02.480 --> 01:14:04.210
What this about a oil tanker?

01:14:04.210 --> 01:14:07.580
It's the letters spelling "she"
that Rachel left behind.

01:14:07.580 --> 01:14:10.840
The word "she"
can also refer to a ship.

01:14:08.000 --> 01:14:08.040
NAKA

01:14:08.000 --> 01:14:08.040
TOMI

01:14:08.130 --> 01:14:08.170
NAKA

01:14:08.130 --> 01:14:08.170
TOMI

01:14:16.780 --> 01:14:19.350
Is what you told me
on the phone true?

01:14:19.350 --> 01:14:23.600
How could everything that's happening
now be part of Leon-sensei's plot?

01:14:23.600 --> 01:14:26.230
I want you to explain
so that I can understand, too.

01:14:26.230 --> 01:14:30.210
It all started with the blue sapphire
that Zhonhan Chen located.

01:14:30.210 --> 01:14:31.730
"The Fist of Blue Sapphire."

01:14:31.730 --> 01:14:35.050
He embedded that into the
belt for the karate tournament...

01:14:35.050 --> 01:14:37.240
And decided to
present it to the champion.

01:14:37.240 --> 01:14:42.370
Leon-san forced Jamaluddin-san
to participate so he could obtain the jewel.

01:14:42.370 --> 01:14:45.770
However, some unexpected
interference entered the picture.

01:14:45.770 --> 01:14:50.310
Kyogoku Makoto, a man who's gone undefeated in 400 karate matches, entered the tournament.

01:14:50.310 --> 01:14:54.380
And Sherilyn Tan-san, who was later killed,
was the one who invited him.

01:14:54.380 --> 01:14:58.860
Even if that <i>was</i> the motive,
Leon-sensei has an alibi.

01:14:58.860 --> 01:15:02.950
He had been riding in a
different elevator when she was stabbed.

01:15:02.950 --> 01:15:04.640
Here's what really happened.

01:15:04.640 --> 01:15:06.910
After meeting Leon by the pool...

01:15:06.910 --> 01:15:11.020
She took the elevator
to go back to her room.

01:15:11.020 --> 01:15:16.280
But the room in she had been
staying in was on the 16th floor of Tower 3.

01:15:16.280 --> 01:15:18.260
Due to the structure of the hotel...

01:15:18.260 --> 01:15:22.030
She couldn't go back without transferring
to a different elevator on the 34th floor.

01:15:22.030 --> 01:15:25.200
While she was on her
way back to her room...

01:15:25.200 --> 01:15:27.960
She was forcibly taken
to a different room...

01:15:27.960 --> 01:15:30.710
By Secretary Rachel.

01:15:30.710 --> 01:15:34.090
No way...
Rachel was an accomplice?!

01:15:34.090 --> 01:15:39.970
The room Leon reserved that day solely
to enter the poolside restaurant for guests...

01:15:39.970 --> 01:15:41.470
Was on the 34th floor.

01:15:42.830 --> 01:15:48.520
Leon came down to that room, and
it was there that he stabbed and killed Sherilyn-san...

01:15:49.440 --> 01:15:51.520
Then placed her body in his suitcase.

01:15:51.520 --> 01:15:55.280
Afterwards, Rachel and Leon
each took separate elevators...

01:15:55.280 --> 01:15:59.550
And for their trick, she probably utilized the type of faux penknife often used in magic.

01:15:59.550 --> 01:16:02.280
However, the blood
was Sherilyn-san's own.

01:16:03.080 --> 01:16:04.330
First floor.

01:16:07.040 --> 01:16:09.790
Pretending to have
been stabbed, Rachel collapsed.

01:16:11.290 --> 01:16:12.580
And immediately afterwards...

01:16:16.070 --> 01:16:21.430
This all went unbeknownst to people in the midst
of the power outage caused by the explosions.

01:16:35.940 --> 01:16:37.820
T-That can't be...

01:16:37.820 --> 01:16:41.720
Knowing of Leon's true plan...

01:16:41.720 --> 01:16:46.220
Rachel came to Detective Mouri out of fear, ready to open up to him about everything.

01:16:46.220 --> 01:16:48.330
And Leon realized that.

01:16:48.330 --> 01:16:52.460
The Rachel-san who came
to the safe room was Kid in disguise.

01:16:52.460 --> 01:16:56.460
Kid was used in Leon-san's plan, too.

01:16:56.460 --> 01:16:59.940
The real Rachel-san
had already been killed...

01:16:59.940 --> 01:17:01.930
And stuffed inside the pedestal.

01:17:02.820 --> 01:17:05.430
Foreseeing that Kid would
come disguised as Rachel-san...

01:17:05.430 --> 01:17:09.680
He did this to create an alibi for himself,
as well as make it look as if it were Kid's doing.

01:17:09.680 --> 01:17:11.790
But why would he do such a thing...?

01:17:11.790 --> 01:17:15.230
Then if it were you, Rishi-san, who would
you think it'd be safe to disguise yourself as?

01:17:15.230 --> 01:17:17.210
Uh, well...

01:17:17.210 --> 01:17:19.120
No matter how
well I disguised myself...

01:17:19.120 --> 01:17:21.990
It'd all be meaningless
if the real person suddenly showed up.

01:17:21.990 --> 01:17:25.490
So it'd be fine if you knew the time
and place the person would be at in advance, right?

01:17:25.490 --> 01:17:26.510
I get it!

01:17:26.510 --> 01:17:29.830
Rachel had been waiting
for Mouri-san at 3 PM...

01:17:29.830 --> 01:17:30.790
And so...

01:17:30.790 --> 01:17:31.770
That's right.

01:17:31.770 --> 01:17:35.350
Kid disguised himself as someone
unlikely to come to the safe room...

01:17:35.350 --> 01:17:39.340
And by doing so,
he fell right into Leon-san's trap.

01:17:40.920 --> 01:17:42.300
Please tell me.

01:17:42.300 --> 01:17:44.820
What is my instructor trying to do?!

01:17:44.820 --> 01:17:47.550
It's all for a foolish plan.

01:17:47.550 --> 01:17:52.230
Leon having been in contact with
Eugene Lim, the leader of a fleet of pirates...

01:17:52.230 --> 01:17:56.730
The word "she" having been left behind
in the pedestal at the scene of Rachel's murder...

01:17:56.730 --> 01:18:00.300
And then there's the object Rachel secretly left with Detective Mouri...

01:18:00.300 --> 01:18:02.070
One of Nakatomi Shipping's tokens.

01:18:02.070 --> 01:18:04.470
All those things point towards a ship.

01:18:04.470 --> 01:18:06.220
What does that
have to do with anything...?

01:18:06.220 --> 01:18:07.160
Rishi-san.

01:18:08.200 --> 01:18:11.350
I had an older detective guy
from Tokyo send me this.

01:18:11.350 --> 01:18:15.040
It's an analysis of the routes that ships
owned by Nakatomi in this area are taking.

01:18:15.730 --> 01:18:19.360
One oil tanker is deviating
greatly from its planned route.

01:18:19.360 --> 01:18:22.920
If it continues along this path,
it'll end up at Marina Bay.

01:18:22.920 --> 01:18:27.930
Leon-san plans on using the pirates
to make the oil tanker crash into the city!

01:18:32.430 --> 01:18:36.620
First of all, why would my
instructor need to do that?

01:18:36.620 --> 01:18:37.730
What reason would he have?!

01:18:37.730 --> 01:18:41.270
I don't know what Leon-san will say...

01:18:41.270 --> 01:18:44.760
But if it's to destroy
this city and then rebuild it...

01:18:44.760 --> 01:18:47.910
Then we at least know for sure that it
involves a vast amount of money moving around.

01:18:47.910 --> 01:18:51.310
The reason Leon was so fixated
on the Fist of Blue Sapphire...

01:18:51.310 --> 01:18:55.160
Is because he needed it as collateral
to manipulate the pirates into doing as he pleases.

01:18:55.160 --> 01:18:56.730
B-But...

01:18:56.730 --> 01:19:00.440
The pirates are scattered all over the place
to avoid the eyes of the police.

01:19:00.440 --> 01:19:02.000
How did he contact them?

01:19:02.000 --> 01:19:04.010
With the Merlion.

01:19:04.010 --> 01:19:07.570
Wasn't there an incident where
the Merlion started spewing red water?

01:19:07.570 --> 01:19:11.370
News of it was broadcast worldwide,
so I'm sure it also caught the attention of the pirates.

01:19:11.370 --> 01:19:14.020
That must have been the signal
to start carrying out the plan.

01:19:14.020 --> 01:19:15.790
But right now, we need to...

01:19:15.790 --> 01:19:18.140
Right.
If we don't hurry, it'll be too late.

01:19:18.140 --> 01:19:20.960
You can say that,
but there's nothing I can do on my own...

01:19:20.960 --> 01:19:24.030
And we'll need more proof
to put the police into action.

01:19:24.030 --> 01:19:25.380
If we do that,
we won't make it in time!

01:19:25.380 --> 01:19:26.820
Isn't there any other way?

01:19:26.820 --> 01:19:29.590
I know.
Let's ask Mr. Zhonhan Chen for advice.

01:19:29.590 --> 01:19:32.030
He holds a lot of influence
over the military and the police.

01:19:32.030 --> 01:19:34.350
I'm sure he'll lend us a hand!

01:19:34.330 --> 01:19:36.040
Rishi-san,
there's just one more thing.

01:19:36.040 --> 01:19:37.540
What is it?

01:19:37.540 --> 01:19:40.810
If the oil tanker crashed into
the city the way he planned...

01:19:40.810 --> 01:19:43.300
Where do you think Leon-san
would be at the time?

01:19:43.300 --> 01:19:47.110
Well, let's see...
My instructor is a very cautious person...

01:19:47.110 --> 01:19:49.700
So he'd probably observe
from somewhere far away.

01:19:49.700 --> 01:19:53.080
There's a chance he may
not even be in the country.

01:19:53.080 --> 01:19:55.060
Okay, I've got to hurry!

01:19:55.580 --> 01:19:58.060
Alright, thanks.

01:20:05.820 --> 01:20:08.420
Oh, come on...
Where could Dad be?

01:20:08.420 --> 01:20:10.630
The show's going to start.

01:20:10.630 --> 01:20:13.830
And Shinichi's still off somewhere...

01:20:15.830 --> 01:20:19.830
Man, how did I get
caught up in this case?

01:20:19.830 --> 01:20:25.440
Was Leon really the one who left my card
at the scene of Sherilyn-san's murder?

01:20:25.440 --> 01:20:26.370
No.

01:20:26.960 --> 01:20:29.950
Finding the card that
had been stuck to the elevator...

01:20:29.950 --> 01:20:32.970
Happened long after
examination of the scene had begun.

01:20:32.970 --> 01:20:34.330
Why do you think that is?

01:20:35.260 --> 01:20:36.490
Oh...

01:20:36.490 --> 01:20:39.480
It's the latest analysis
of the oil tanker's trajectory.

01:20:39.480 --> 01:20:40.540
Huh?!

01:20:41.390 --> 01:20:42.600
W-What?!

01:20:42.600 --> 01:20:43.690
This is really bad!

01:20:43.690 --> 01:20:45.360
At this rate, the oil tanker
will crash right into the hotel!

01:21:06.920 --> 01:21:09.630
Ran...
Please pick up the phone!

01:21:52.630 --> 01:21:54.050
It's heading this way!

01:22:39.100 --> 01:22:41.820
Hey, Ran!
Are you enjoying yourself?

01:22:41.820 --> 01:22:43.700
Dad!
Where are you right now?!

01:22:43.700 --> 01:22:44.350
Huh?

01:22:44.350 --> 01:22:48.350
I dunno what it is,
but I can see some really big ship.

01:22:48.350 --> 01:22:50.880
Hey...
Wait a minute, Dad...

01:22:50.880 --> 01:22:52.610
Don't tell me you're
at the top of the hotel?!

01:22:52.610 --> 01:22:52.650
Mouri Ran

01:22:52.610 --> 01:22:52.650
Call in Progress

01:22:52.610 --> 01:22:54.610
Hello? Hello?!

01:22:59.870 --> 01:23:01.030
Can we make it?

01:23:01.330 --> 01:23:02.330
I think so.

01:23:02.620 --> 01:23:04.950
Sonoko-san! Sonoko-san!

01:23:05.620 --> 01:23:06.640
What?

01:23:06.640 --> 01:23:08.350
It seems something
has happened outside.

01:23:08.350 --> 01:23:10.360
I thought it might be best
to leave the hotel.

01:23:14.400 --> 01:23:15.880
Yes?

01:23:15.880 --> 01:23:17.780
Okay, I understand.

01:23:17.780 --> 01:23:19.320
Who was that from?

01:23:19.320 --> 01:23:20.640
Someone from the police.

01:23:20.640 --> 01:23:24.060
He said I may be targeted again
if I carelessly went outside...

01:23:24.060 --> 01:23:25.640
So I should standby
and wait in my room.

01:23:25.640 --> 01:23:27.980
It looks like someone
is coming to escort me.

01:23:30.060 --> 01:23:31.750
B-But...

01:23:31.750 --> 01:23:34.360
I'll be fine because I'm here.

01:23:36.130 --> 01:23:37.320
I understand.

01:23:47.020 --> 01:23:47.810
This is bad...

01:23:47.810 --> 01:23:49.960
We can't get close to
the hotel with this crowd of people!

01:23:49.960 --> 01:23:52.500
This is do-or-die,
so I guess I'll have to do this!

01:23:56.940 --> 01:23:58.680
Whoa, it's Kid!

01:23:59.220 --> 01:24:01.680
It's Kid! Kid's here!

01:24:06.040 --> 01:24:08.020
With this, it's like
it's reserved just for us!

01:24:08.020 --> 01:24:08.810
H-Huh?

01:24:08.810 --> 01:24:10.330
W-What's the problem?!

01:24:10.330 --> 01:24:11.810
What?

01:24:11.810 --> 01:24:14.940
T-The Sleeping Kogoro!

01:24:23.870 --> 01:24:26.200
I really don't know, just about him...

01:24:28.960 --> 01:24:30.830
It's no good.
It won't go through.

01:24:36.400 --> 01:24:37.590
Whoa, crap!

01:24:45.410 --> 01:24:48.310
Oh, come on...
Where are you, Dad?!

01:24:58.480 --> 01:24:59.320
Look!

01:24:59.990 --> 01:25:02.160
This city will be born again!

01:25:02.450 --> 01:25:03.870
With my hands!

01:25:06.870 --> 01:25:08.370
Why... are you...?

01:25:18.280 --> 01:25:19.460
W-Wait!

01:25:21.920 --> 01:25:22.970
I'm surprised.

01:25:22.970 --> 01:25:26.370
I never thought you'd
be able to make it this far.

01:25:26.370 --> 01:25:28.260
Even I couldn't
read this far into you.

01:25:30.450 --> 01:25:31.730
Rishi.

01:25:31.730 --> 01:25:34.710
But now that it's come to this,
I'll acknowledge your integrity.

01:25:34.710 --> 01:25:37.230
That's right.
This is all my plan.

01:25:37.230 --> 01:25:39.420
Why don't we talk this over a bit?

01:25:39.420 --> 01:25:41.740
So put that
dangerous thing away.

01:25:42.510 --> 01:25:45.990
Aren't <i>you</i> the one who's
misunderstanding something, Leon-sensei?

01:25:47.950 --> 01:25:49.120
Freeze!

01:25:51.370 --> 01:25:52.540
There's no one here...

01:25:52.540 --> 01:25:54.000
Let's stop the ship now.

01:26:14.140 --> 01:26:16.380
The oil tanker stopped, Kid!

01:26:16.380 --> 01:26:18.090
Let's leave this to the police!

01:26:18.090 --> 01:26:18.730
Yeah.

01:26:19.480 --> 01:26:20.530
The tanker!

01:26:20.820 --> 01:26:22.070
What happened...?

01:26:22.740 --> 01:26:24.380
I'll do whatever you say...

01:26:24.380 --> 01:26:25.760
Just please don't shoot me!

01:26:26.950 --> 01:26:28.240
Ah, help me...!

01:26:28.240 --> 01:26:31.260
Please don't kill me!

01:26:31.990 --> 01:26:35.250
Rishi-kun...
I never thought you'd actually shoot.

01:26:35.250 --> 01:26:36.250
Jamaluddin!

01:26:37.630 --> 01:26:38.380
Wait!

01:26:39.040 --> 01:26:40.750
Jamaluddin, what are you thinking?!

01:26:41.050 --> 01:26:42.960
The only reason I worked for you...

01:26:42.960 --> 01:26:44.970
Was to fight against Kyogoku.

01:26:44.970 --> 01:26:47.300
I have no such reason anymore.

01:26:47.550 --> 01:26:48.260
What?!

01:26:48.260 --> 01:26:49.390
Leon-sensei...

01:26:49.390 --> 01:26:52.890
Pardon my rudeness,
but have your skills gotten a little rusty?

01:26:52.890 --> 01:26:55.890
You're not the one
who was putting the world in motion...

01:26:58.880 --> 01:27:00.150
I was.

01:27:00.150 --> 01:27:03.150
You couldn't possibly have...

01:27:03.780 --> 01:27:04.900
W-Wait...

01:27:04.900 --> 01:27:06.610
Please wait...

01:27:06.610 --> 01:27:08.320
I'll give you this.

01:27:08.320 --> 01:27:12.030
There's a jewel inside.
Isn't that a fair deal, Rishi-kun?

01:27:25.110 --> 01:27:26.800
Kaito Kid!

01:27:26.800 --> 01:27:30.220
W-What is Arthur-kun doing here?!

01:27:30.720 --> 01:27:31.640
Let's see...

01:27:31.640 --> 01:27:34.470
To get to the roof, I think
I have to transfer at the 34th floor.

01:27:34.350 --> 01:27:35.930
34th floor.

01:27:36.100 --> 01:27:36.890
Hey!

01:27:37.350 --> 01:27:38.230
Wait.

01:27:49.910 --> 01:27:50.660
Are they...

01:27:50.660 --> 01:27:53.080
Heading towards Marina Bay Sands?!

01:27:57.080 --> 01:27:58.310
What are you doing?!

01:27:58.310 --> 01:28:01.860
I was trying to catch those two,
who were the masterminds behind this!

01:28:01.860 --> 01:28:04.590
Stop with the poor acting,
Rishi Ramanathan.

01:28:04.590 --> 01:28:08.090
I know full well
that <i>you </i>are the mastermind.

01:28:08.090 --> 01:28:10.110
The first thing that made
me have my doubts about you...

01:28:10.110 --> 01:28:13.070
Was Kid's advance notice
that was left at the crime scene.

01:28:13.070 --> 01:28:15.540
The police didn't notice
the advance notice...

01:28:15.540 --> 01:28:19.350
Until right after you arrived
at the scene, did they, Rishi?

01:28:19.350 --> 01:28:22.790
And earlier, when I asked you
where Leon-san would be...

01:28:22.790 --> 01:28:25.110
My doubts towards you solidified.

01:28:25.110 --> 01:28:26.360
What?!

01:28:26.360 --> 01:28:29.380
Someone as conceited
and self-centered as Leon-san...

01:28:29.380 --> 01:28:32.870
Would never flee the country
when the success of his plan was close at hand.

01:28:32.870 --> 01:28:37.700
I'm certain he would be in a place with the best view, watching it all happen.

01:28:37.700 --> 01:28:40.250
And you couldn't possibly
have not been aware of that!

01:28:41.390 --> 01:28:42.540
Well, this is surprising.

01:28:42.540 --> 01:28:44.520
So you were just
testing me with that, huh?

01:28:44.520 --> 01:28:46.250
It all started five years ago...

01:28:46.250 --> 01:28:49.760
And your father's accident was
the beginning of your plan, wasn't it?

01:28:49.760 --> 01:28:54.260
"Suspect Admits Killing
Oceanographer After Initial Denial."

01:28:54.260 --> 01:28:55.810
Unless I'm mistaken...

01:28:57.450 --> 01:29:01.460
Nakatomi-san also first came
to Singapore five years ago, correct?

01:29:01.460 --> 01:29:03.270
N-No, I...

01:29:03.270 --> 01:29:05.730
Leon-san caught the killer...

01:29:05.730 --> 01:29:08.780
While Sherilyn-san acted as his attorney
and made him admit to his guilt.

01:29:08.780 --> 01:29:11.280
I can't think that's
a mere coincidence.

01:29:11.280 --> 01:29:13.050
What do you mean?

01:29:13.050 --> 01:29:17.540
It was a trap set in order to obtain
the oil tanker owned by Nakatomi Shipping.

01:29:17.540 --> 01:29:20.040
Everything was planned.

01:29:20.040 --> 01:29:24.310
And then there was one more trap...

01:29:24.310 --> 01:29:27.400
The fact of which you
realized, didn't you?

01:29:27.400 --> 01:29:31.090
I also thought
it was an accident at first, but...

01:29:31.090 --> 01:29:34.050
As I was sorting through my father's personal effects, I realized...

01:29:34.050 --> 01:29:38.560
That as my father was investigating some underwater ruins, he had coincidentally discovered...

01:29:38.560 --> 01:29:43.350
A sunken ship where the Fist of Blue Sapphire, the emblem of the king of all pirates, was likely to be resting.

01:29:43.350 --> 01:29:46.710
That's why you
started by killing my father!

01:29:46.710 --> 01:29:50.440
To prevent him from
recovering the jewel first!

01:29:50.820 --> 01:29:51.820
Help!

01:29:51.820 --> 01:29:53.450
Someone pushed me in the back!

01:29:55.780 --> 01:29:57.120
Help is on the way!

01:29:57.120 --> 01:29:57.910
Hurry!

01:29:57.910 --> 01:29:59.200
Save him!

01:29:59.200 --> 01:30:01.220
Since my father had
a strong sense of justice...

01:30:01.220 --> 01:30:04.710
I'm sure you guessed that he
would definitely dive in to save him.

01:30:13.990 --> 01:30:16.730
W-What is the
meaning of this, Leon?!

01:30:16.730 --> 01:30:17.660
You—

01:30:17.660 --> 01:30:18.930
Let go of me!

01:30:21.240 --> 01:30:25.000
Rishi-kun,
you're misunderstanding something.

01:30:25.000 --> 01:30:27.400
The one who killed your father
was sent to prison—

01:30:27.400 --> 01:30:29.650
Having suspected you
of causing my father's death...

01:30:29.650 --> 01:30:33.210
I came to this country, became your pupil,
and became a reserve officer.

01:30:33.210 --> 01:30:36.180
Then I began
investigating into the accident.

01:30:36.180 --> 01:30:39.280
I became acquainted with Sherilyn Tan,
who had been in charge of defending him.

01:30:39.280 --> 01:30:43.080
When I approached her, asking if she had any info
about the case on Reijiro that could shake up Leon...

01:30:43.080 --> 01:30:45.020
She told me briefly.

01:30:45.020 --> 01:30:46.520
And then there was Rachel.

01:30:46.520 --> 01:30:47.460
That's right.

01:30:47.460 --> 01:30:52.090
Every bit of information on you
was leaked to me through her!

01:30:53.150 --> 01:30:56.610
In that case, why did you
post an advance notice from Kid?

01:30:56.610 --> 01:30:59.010
How about you tell us?

01:30:59.010 --> 01:31:03.870
There's the Fist of Blue Sapphire,
and then a murder case he had nothing to do with.

01:31:03.870 --> 01:31:07.370
If I dangled those two things in front of him,
I knew for sure the phantom thief would come.

01:31:07.370 --> 01:31:10.270
And then he would get
in the way of your plan for me.

01:31:11.400 --> 01:31:14.650
That high school detective
didn't show up like I had planned...

01:31:14.650 --> 01:31:17.660
But you played your role well.

01:31:17.660 --> 01:31:23.370
Nakatomi-san, it seems Leon-san saved you
right when you were being suspected of theft...

01:31:23.370 --> 01:31:25.930
But is that <i>really </i>just a coincidence?

01:31:25.930 --> 01:31:31.000
Think things over well.
What if this was all just a part of his...

01:31:32.900 --> 01:31:34.150
You bastard!

01:31:35.210 --> 01:31:38.320
You really did
your research, Rishi-kun.

01:31:42.580 --> 01:31:44.560
Huh?
Where am I?

01:31:44.560 --> 01:31:46.080
If I remember right...

01:31:46.080 --> 01:31:47.460
Dad!

01:31:47.460 --> 01:31:48.520
Huh?

01:31:48.520 --> 01:31:49.120
Oh!

01:31:51.040 --> 01:31:52.270
A-Ah!

01:31:52.270 --> 01:31:53.380
Ran?!

01:31:53.380 --> 01:31:54.610
What?!

01:31:59.410 --> 01:32:00.260
W-What the...?!

01:32:00.260 --> 01:32:01.620
Dad...

01:32:04.450 --> 01:32:04.990
Ra—

01:32:06.910 --> 01:32:07.790
Fall back!

01:32:07.790 --> 01:32:10.170
And regroup! Tell the chopper, too!

01:32:14.070 --> 01:32:15.920
Who are you guys?

01:32:17.170 --> 01:32:18.420
Now then, Rishi-kun...

01:32:18.420 --> 01:32:21.640
Unfortunately for you,
the tables have turned.

01:32:21.640 --> 01:32:24.350
Eugene, the plan seems to have failed.

01:32:24.640 --> 01:32:26.310
You can take this jewel.

01:32:26.520 --> 01:32:29.100
Take care of anyone here.

01:32:34.230 --> 01:32:35.650
What are you doing?!

01:32:36.190 --> 01:32:37.190
Don't move!

01:32:39.070 --> 01:32:41.070
H-Help me!

01:32:41.070 --> 01:32:44.780
Now that I have the jewel, I have no need for you.

01:32:44.780 --> 01:32:45.620
What?

01:32:46.330 --> 01:32:49.500
I have no time for your nonsense.

01:32:49.500 --> 01:32:52.250
I am known to break promises.

01:32:52.250 --> 01:32:55.540
It's just that there was a more lucrative offer.

01:32:56.130 --> 01:32:58.460
Don't tell me you guys are after...

01:32:59.690 --> 01:33:02.000
You sure are observant, kid.

01:33:02.000 --> 01:33:03.050
That's it exactly.

01:33:03.050 --> 01:33:06.660
The daughter of the
Suzuki Financial Group is in this hotel.

01:33:06.660 --> 01:33:09.560
And if we kidnap her,
the ransom we can get will be astronomical.

01:33:09.560 --> 01:33:12.750
Hasn't the little lady
already taken shelter?

01:33:12.750 --> 01:33:14.560
She should still be in her suite.

01:33:14.560 --> 01:33:18.570
Because I told her over the phone
to absolutely not leave her room.

01:33:21.820 --> 01:33:23.590
W-Wait...
Makoto-san?!

01:33:23.590 --> 01:33:24.570
Excuse me for doing this!

01:33:24.570 --> 01:33:25.600
Wha—?!

01:33:25.600 --> 01:33:27.520
All the elevators have been stopped.

01:33:27.540 --> 01:33:28.200
What?!

01:33:28.200 --> 01:33:29.660
Let's get out of here.

01:33:32.670 --> 01:33:34.040
There! Come on!

01:33:34.790 --> 01:33:36.840
Don't shoot! You'll hit her!

01:33:36.840 --> 01:33:40.150
M-Makoto-san...
What's going on here?

01:33:46.600 --> 01:33:47.600
Look.

01:33:47.600 --> 01:33:51.230
Everything will work out
just as I pictured in the end.

01:33:51.230 --> 01:33:53.600
This city will be burned
to the ground, and be born again!

01:34:02.050 --> 01:34:04.280
But you won't be alive to see it!

01:34:09.410 --> 01:34:11.660
What?! They're going to shoot rockets at us?

01:34:25.860 --> 01:34:26.220
Whoa...

01:34:29.930 --> 01:34:30.810
Damn them!

01:34:34.850 --> 01:34:36.000
Take this!

01:34:37.770 --> 01:34:39.060
Get them, now!

01:34:40.170 --> 01:34:41.230
Makoto-san!

01:34:48.470 --> 01:34:51.080
What?!
Wh-Wh-What are you...?!

01:34:51.290 --> 01:34:52.120
After them!

01:34:56.830 --> 01:34:57.880
Open up!

01:34:57.440 --> 01:34:59.590
They're here! They're here!
They're here! They're here!

01:34:57.880 --> 01:34:59.000
You brats!

01:35:04.650 --> 01:35:06.650
What is going on here?

01:35:06.630 --> 01:35:07.590
I don't know.

01:35:07.590 --> 01:35:09.890
Most of the pirates are now in the hotel.

01:35:09.890 --> 01:35:11.930
Just what is going on inside?

01:35:11.930 --> 01:35:14.600
It's dangerous here, too. Please get back.

01:35:44.210 --> 01:35:45.700
Are you okay?

01:35:45.700 --> 01:35:46.860
Y-Yeah...

01:35:46.860 --> 01:35:49.800
If this keeps up,
the city really will be destroyed!

01:35:51.180 --> 01:35:53.680
Damn it!
Isn't there any good way to stop this?

01:35:55.680 --> 01:35:58.410
If we could use that,
we could pull this off!

01:35:58.410 --> 01:35:59.690
Kid!

01:36:01.380 --> 01:36:03.320
Wait...
Are you serious?!

01:36:03.320 --> 01:36:04.070
Of course I am!

01:36:07.920 --> 01:36:09.240
It's the guy again!

01:36:09.240 --> 01:36:10.410
Shoot him down!

01:36:12.070 --> 01:36:13.410
Boss, we can't hit him!

01:36:13.410 --> 01:36:15.080
Pesky little bird!

01:36:17.680 --> 01:36:21.580
Hey, we've got to do something about that group of pirates before we can do your plan...

01:36:21.580 --> 01:36:23.860
And my playing card gun's
only got one more shot!

01:36:23.860 --> 01:36:25.480
Isn't there one way left?

01:36:25.480 --> 01:36:26.210
Huh?

01:36:29.860 --> 01:36:32.220
A trump card that'll turn
the tables with a single shot!

01:36:32.220 --> 01:36:33.850
I get it!

01:36:34.530 --> 01:36:35.560
I'm diving in close!

01:36:36.640 --> 01:36:37.220
Wait!

01:36:56.410 --> 01:36:57.660
Makoto-san...?!

01:37:00.750 --> 01:37:01.460
Get them!

01:37:03.920 --> 01:37:05.090
Stay back!

01:37:07.090 --> 01:37:08.630
He is...

01:37:10.920 --> 01:37:12.010
...mine!

01:37:12.590 --> 01:37:13.330
Kid...

01:37:13.330 --> 01:37:13.930
Oh?

01:37:13.930 --> 01:37:15.680
Take me to the bow of the ship!

01:37:16.390 --> 01:37:18.060
You don't have to tell me twice!

01:37:18.060 --> 01:37:18.810
Whoa!

01:37:22.670 --> 01:37:24.440
Ran, stay back!

01:37:25.900 --> 01:37:27.690
Ran!

01:37:31.470 --> 01:37:33.860
Go!

01:37:48.820 --> 01:37:50.400
What in the
world is going on here?!

01:37:50.400 --> 01:37:52.530
I heard Shinichi's voice...

01:37:52.530 --> 01:37:54.360
Are you okay, Miss?

01:37:54.360 --> 01:37:56.570
Arthur-kun...
What are you doing here?

01:37:56.570 --> 01:37:59.680
Ah...
I was worried about you, Miss.

01:37:59.680 --> 01:38:01.660
Thanks.

01:38:02.410 --> 01:38:05.190
Oh, come on!
Where is he?!

01:38:07.690 --> 01:38:09.110
I'm glad you're safe.

01:38:10.530 --> 01:38:11.380
What?

01:38:14.970 --> 01:38:16.870
Thank you!

01:38:21.160 --> 01:38:22.000
Makoto-san!

01:38:22.790 --> 01:38:24.710
Kid took the jewel.

01:38:24.710 --> 01:38:26.500
Can you shoot him down?

01:38:26.710 --> 01:38:27.960
OK, boss.

01:38:34.800 --> 01:38:37.010
Damn! Stay still...

01:38:37.300 --> 01:38:38.350
Take this!

01:38:41.660 --> 01:38:42.500
Huh?

01:38:44.160 --> 01:38:45.020
Was he on the mark?

01:38:46.940 --> 01:38:48.400
It will be fine, Sonoko-san!

01:38:52.940 --> 01:38:53.860
Oh, no...

01:38:54.240 --> 01:38:54.820
What?

01:38:55.610 --> 01:38:56.190
Kid!

01:38:56.320 --> 01:38:57.030
You...!

01:38:57.390 --> 01:38:58.410
Hi!

01:38:58.950 --> 01:38:59.580
Wait!

01:39:07.210 --> 01:39:08.380
Help me, man!

01:39:09.170 --> 01:39:10.500
I'm falling down!

01:39:11.980 --> 01:39:13.510
Makoto-san, you're bleeding!

01:39:13.510 --> 01:39:16.650
Sonoko-san,
please excuse me for this!

01:39:16.650 --> 01:39:19.090
Huh?!
Wait, what are you doing?

01:39:19.090 --> 01:39:21.850
We're out in a
place like this... Makoto-san?!

01:39:21.850 --> 01:39:23.310
I'm telling you no!

01:39:23.310 --> 01:39:24.350
What?! Ah!

01:39:27.040 --> 01:39:28.740
It's a back-carry knot.

01:39:28.740 --> 01:39:34.230
Sonoko-san, make absolutely sure
you stay close to me this time!

01:39:35.570 --> 01:39:39.240
I couldn't get away from
you like this, even if I wanted to...

01:40:22.660 --> 01:40:23.910
Where is he?!

01:40:52.420 --> 01:40:53.480
Kyogoku-san!

01:40:53.480 --> 01:40:55.480
Hold onto something!

01:41:38.650 --> 01:41:39.900
Are you alright?

01:41:50.730 --> 01:41:51.960
You can have this back.

01:41:51.960 --> 01:41:52.910
Huh?

01:41:54.120 --> 01:41:55.170
That...

01:41:55.170 --> 01:41:57.920
Wasn't the jewel I'm looking for.

01:42:06.570 --> 01:42:10.310
Sonoko-san...
Please sit down here for a while.

01:42:10.310 --> 01:42:12.430
I apologize.

01:42:12.430 --> 01:42:14.940
It's knotted a little too tightly...

01:42:19.670 --> 01:42:21.490
Ah, it came loose.

01:42:22.720 --> 01:42:26.140
Ah, no!
No, that's... Um...

01:42:26.140 --> 01:42:28.600
That's something...
like a good luck charm.

01:42:28.600 --> 01:42:31.080
Did you always have this on you?

01:42:31.080 --> 01:42:32.930
Y-Yes...

01:42:32.930 --> 01:42:36.420
Though I couldn't come out and tell you,
thinking I'd lose my pride as a man.

01:42:37.400 --> 01:42:38.730
So that's it...

01:42:38.730 --> 01:42:40.840
I always thought
he was being protected...

01:42:40.840 --> 01:42:44.840
But it looks like I was
the one protecting Makoto-san.

01:42:52.100 --> 01:42:53.730
So that's it! So that's it!

01:42:53.730 --> 01:42:55.410
Please return my band-aid to me!

01:42:55.410 --> 01:42:56.480
No way!

01:42:56.480 --> 01:42:57.100
Please!

01:42:57.100 --> 01:42:59.250
I'm going to treasure it
for the rest of my life!

01:42:59.250 --> 01:43:00.860
They're a lovely couple, aren't they?

01:43:09.010 --> 01:43:12.120
Who in the world are you?

01:43:12.120 --> 01:43:14.870
You're not some ordinary kid, are you?

01:43:16.940 --> 01:43:21.420
I'm Edogawa Conan, a detective.

01:43:22.420 --> 01:43:24.050
...is the one true answer I try to unravel and make...

01:43:24.800 --> 01:43:26.970
...a mysterious illusion hidden in those hands of yours?

01:43:28.140 --> 01:43:31.260
Like a blue sapphire floating in the night sky.

01:43:32.100 --> 01:43:33.720
...is the fate I've been drawn towards...

01:43:34.350 --> 01:43:37.850
...and I come across it every time it glistens?

01:43:37.850 --> 01:43:41.520
Like a blue sapphire floating in the night sky.

01:43:44.480 --> 01:43:46.360
Secret in the moonlight

01:43:47.030 --> 01:43:48.910
Secret in the moonlight

01:43:50.490 --> 01:43:55.370
A mirage of you wavers in the panoramic sunset...

01:43:55.830 --> 01:44:00.040
Seducing me into sleepless nights.

01:44:00.380 --> 01:44:04.920
The flavor and rhythm of the city scene heat up...

01:44:05.510 --> 01:44:09.720
Sending my heart racing with burning anticipation.

01:44:09.970 --> 01:44:13.180
So that the moonlight will illuminate the night...

01:44:13.180 --> 01:44:14.640
And we stumble across each other on the flip side... (Flip side)

01:44:14.640 --> 01:44:19.600
I'll dance with these playfully wavering shadows.

01:44:20.560 --> 01:44:22.230
...is the one true answer I try to unravel and make...

01:44:22.900 --> 01:44:25.150
...a mysterious illusion hidden in those hands of yours?

01:44:26.230 --> 01:44:29.360
Like a blue sapphire floating in the night sky.

01:44:30.320 --> 01:44:31.820
...is the fate I've been drawn towards...

01:44:32.570 --> 01:44:35.950
...and I come across it every time it glistens?

01:44:35.950 --> 01:44:39.620
Like a blue sapphire floating in the night sky.

01:44:42.630 --> 01:44:44.510
Secret in the moonlight

01:44:48.720 --> 01:44:51.130
The dilemma of playing these games...

01:44:51.550 --> 01:44:58.180
Is like a stark white rose thorn, preventing us from coming together.

01:44:58.600 --> 01:45:03.150
And the longer this feeling doesn't reach you, the more fired up it gets.

01:45:03.610 --> 01:45:07.860
So extend your hand within the mirror.

01:45:08.190 --> 01:45:11.610
Close your eyes so that your heart opens...

01:45:11.610 --> 01:45:13.160
And we overlap on the flip side... (Flip side)

01:45:13.160 --> 01:45:16.910
Then we'll both picture the same dream.

01:45:18.870 --> 01:45:20.460
...is the one true answer I try to unravel and make...

01:45:21.160 --> 01:45:23.170
...a mysterious illusion hidden in those hands of yours?

01:45:24.380 --> 01:45:27.630
Like a blue sapphire floating in the night sky.

01:45:28.460 --> 01:45:29.970
...is the fate I've been drawn towards...

01:45:30.670 --> 01:45:33.970
...and I come across it every time it glistens?

01:45:34.260 --> 01:45:37.640
Like a blue sapphire floating in the night sky.

01:45:40.850 --> 01:45:42.730
Secret in the moonlight

01:46:07.540 --> 01:46:10.960
As though the sky were studded with jewelry...

01:46:12.340 --> 01:46:14.220
On this night of a blue moon.

01:46:15.470 --> 01:46:20.640
I'm guided towards your dazzlingness...

01:46:21.100 --> 01:46:25.020
The only of it's kind in this blinding city.

01:46:26.650 --> 01:46:28.270
...is the one true answer I try to unravel and make...

01:46:28.940 --> 01:46:31.070
...a mysterious illusion hidden in those hands of yours?

01:46:32.400 --> 01:46:35.530
Like a blue sapphire floating in the night sky.

01:46:36.200 --> 01:46:38.030
...is the fate I've been drawn towards...

01:46:38.580 --> 01:46:41.790
...and I come across it every time it glistens?

01:46:42.040 --> 01:46:45.460
Like a blue sapphire floating in the night sky.

01:46:48.670 --> 01:46:50.550
Secret in the moonlight

01:47:12.730 --> 01:47:14.740
But are you really okay...

01:47:14.740 --> 01:47:18.430
With letting that insanely strong
boyfriend of yours go off to the US again?

01:47:18.430 --> 01:47:19.740
It's fine! It's fine!

01:47:19.740 --> 01:47:23.240
Makoto-san really has to
fight somewhere, doesn't he?

01:47:24.750 --> 01:47:26.690
Oh, they came out!

01:47:26.690 --> 01:47:28.250
Hey...
What's that?

01:47:28.250 --> 01:47:30.960
Come on...
Don't cling to me so tightly.

01:47:30.960 --> 01:47:32.150
Doesn't that make it hard to walk?

01:47:32.150 --> 01:47:35.240
No way.
I'm never letting go of you again.

01:47:35.240 --> 01:47:36.420
Oh, is that right?

01:47:38.070 --> 01:47:40.640
I've been waiting all this time...

01:47:40.640 --> 01:47:41.810
For this moment.

01:47:41.810 --> 01:47:42.260
Huh?

01:47:43.390 --> 01:47:45.390
Kid!
We've been waiting for you!

01:47:45.390 --> 01:47:46.750
What...
Are you serious?!

01:47:46.750 --> 01:47:50.250
I could tell that you
weren't Shinichi right from the start!

01:47:50.250 --> 01:47:51.270
You see, Shinichi...

01:47:51.270 --> 01:47:54.280
Would never do something
like calling my dad "old man"!

01:47:54.280 --> 01:47:56.280
What?!
But he's always...

01:47:57.070 --> 01:47:57.780
Come to think of it...

01:47:57.780 --> 01:48:00.660
I've never called him
"old man" in front of Ran, have I?

01:48:00.660 --> 01:48:03.830
I won't let you off the hook for
pretending to be Shinichi not just once, but twice!

01:48:03.830 --> 01:48:06.660
Young lady, please make
absolutely sure you don't let go of his arm!

01:48:06.660 --> 01:48:08.540
Restrain him!

01:48:11.440 --> 01:48:12.540
Kid!

01:48:12.540 --> 01:48:14.800
Catch him!

01:48:14.800 --> 01:48:17.050
I'm absolutely not going to let go!

01:48:17.050 --> 01:48:18.800
Don't let him get away!

01:48:19.880 --> 01:48:20.810
Professor...

01:48:27.830 --> 01:48:29.310
He's not here!

01:48:32.020 --> 01:48:34.360
Augh!
He got away!

01:48:34.360 --> 01:48:35.370
Damn it!

01:48:35.370 --> 01:48:37.070
He has to still be nearby!

01:48:37.070 --> 01:48:39.030
After him!

01:48:44.100 --> 01:48:45.560
Conan-kun!

01:48:45.560 --> 01:48:48.330
Welcome home, Ran-neechan.

01:48:49.270 --> 01:48:50.330
Good to be back!

01:48:51.650 --> 01:48:53.330
You weren't lonely
without me, were you?

01:48:53.860 --> 01:48:55.400
You dummy...

01:48:55.400 --> 01:49:00.680
We were together the entire time.

01:49:00.880 --> 01:49:05.850
